    <item>
      <title>2024 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2024/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Sep 2024 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2024/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;2024-arin-community-grant-program-recipients&#34;&gt;2024 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped table-bordered js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;caption&gt;2024 Applications&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Applications&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Type&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;1 association, 3 corporations, 3 nonprofits, 1 other &lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Region&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;3 United States, 1 Canada, 4 outside ARIN region&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Category (some projects identified multiple categories)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;3 Internet technical improvements, 3 registry processes and technology improvements, 5 informational outreach, 5 research&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$89,950&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Average funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$11,245&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Projects selected to receive a grant&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding provided (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$40,000&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Project summaries provided by grant recipients.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Search ROAs by ROA Name</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-14/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 Aug 2024 09:45:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-14/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;28 August 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.14 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN add the capability for customers to search the ROAs associated with their organization by ROA name (text). We agree that this would be a useful expansion to the current ROA search options, and we will add it to our list of RPKI improvements pending prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your suggestion will remain open until this new functionality is developed and deployed. Thank you for participating in ARIN’s Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Optional &#34;Geofeed&#34; Field to Whois</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-10/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Jun 2024 02:45:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-10/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7 Jun 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.10 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN add an optional attribute to the Whois database for customers to publish and share their Geofeed URL.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The five Regional Internet Registries (RIRs) are collaborating and working within the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) on a standard &lt;a href=&#34;https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-regext-rdap-geofeed/&#34;&gt;Registry Data Access Protocol (RDAP) extension for Geofeed data&lt;/a&gt;. When the standard is accepted, ARIN will implement this change to RDAP and add the necessary functionality to ARIN Online and Reg-RWS to support this improvement. The other RIRs will also be implementing this change, which will result in a globally consistent method to publish Geofeed information in RDAP.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Increase Length Limit on IRR Remarks Field</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-08/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 May 2024 09:07:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-08/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 June 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.8 upon confirmed receipt, asking that we increase the length limit on the IRR remarks field.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree that this would be a useful improvement that would assist in the transition to ARIN&amp;rsquo;s authenticated IRR from another third-party IRR. ARIN will consider your suggestion in conjunction with other IRR improvements that are in our development pipeline. Your suggestion will remain open until a decision is made on when the features you have requested can be developed. Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Create Mandatory Mailing List for General Members</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-07/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Apr 2024 09:07:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-07/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 May 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.7 upon confirmed receipt, recommending that ARIN automatically subscribe General Members to a mailing list as a requirement of General Membership. From 1999 to 2021, ARIN operated the ARIN Discussion mailing list as an auto-subscribed list for all ARIN member organizations. Since this list’s retirement in 2021, ARIN has adopted the position of all our mailing lists being opt-in only. This change was made to respect member preferences and privacy, ensuring that all subscribers are genuinely interested in the content and fostering more engaged and meaningful discussions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>IRR Service Improvement - Various ARIN Web UI Enhancements</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-05/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 01 Mar 2024 09:07:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-05/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;25 March 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.05 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN enable search and sorting tools for the IRR web interface, as well as the ability to download the full list route objects or what is displayed on the current page in a CSV format. ARIN agrees that these would be useful improvements for IRR users.  There is a similar web UI feature to what you describe in our development pipeline awaiting prioritization and scheduling.  The suggestion for a downloadable report will be reviewed for potential prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RPKI Service Improvement - Various ROA UI Enhancements</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-04/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 01 Mar 2024 09:05:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-04/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;25 March 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.04 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN enable the ability to sort the ROA list page by each field in ascending and descending order, as well as the ability to download the full list or current page in a CSV format. ARIN agrees that these would be useful improvements for RPKI users.  There is a similar web UI feature to what you describe in our development pipeline awaiting prioritization and scheduling.  The suggestion for a downloadable report will be reviewed for potential prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RPKI Service Improvement - ROA Analyze</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-02/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 01 Mar 2024 09:02:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-02/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11 March 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.02 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN add a feature to our RPKI web interface to analyze any negative and potentially unexpected results of creating a ROA, as well as an option to download or export the list of candidate prefixes/ASNs in a CSV format for additional analysis prior to committing changes. There is a similar web UI feature to what you describe in our development pipeline awaiting prioritization and scheduling. The suggestion for a downloadable report will be reviewed for potential prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Multi-factor authentication option for API keys</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-01/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 05 Jan 2024 09:02:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2024/2024-01/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 January 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2024.1 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN implement some form of multi-factor authentication (MFA) for API keys. ARIN agrees that this would be a good improvement to the security of ARIN systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will investigate the requirements to build this new feature and schedule it for future development. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improve ROA Details for Hosted RPKI Product</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-20/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 18 Dec 2023 09:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-20/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 February 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.20 upon confirmed receipt, asking that we improve the ROA details that are displayed in ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Hosted RPKI Service.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will consider your suggestion alongside other RPKI improvements that are in our development pipeline. Your suggestion will remain open until a decision is made on the features you have requested. Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Expand Fraud Reporting to Include Leasing of 4.10 Space</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-18/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Oct 2023 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-18/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;31 October 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.18 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN widen the scope of our fraud reporting tool to include misuse of IPv4 address space acquired using NRPM 4.10. Dedicated IPv4 Block to Facilitate IPv6 Deployment.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We are in the process of evaluating and updating ARIN Fraud Reporting process and procedures, and your feedback will be taken into consideration during this effort. Your suggestion will remain open pending the outcome of the Fraud Process review.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Specified Description of API Keys</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-15/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Oct 2023 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-15/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;27 October 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023-15 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN provide the ability to allow users to specify a description of an API key to make it easier to track the functionality of each key. ARIN agrees that this would be a useful for customers who have multiple API keys.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will add this to our deployment schedule and prioritize it along with other development initiatives. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>REST API Method to Determine a Specific NET Object for a Range</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-13/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 Sep 2023 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-13/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9 October 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.13 upon confirmed receipt, asking ARIN to develop a REST API method to determine the most specific NET object for a range. We are evaluating the work needed to develop this functionality and plan to conduct a consultation to determine the value of this feature to the ARIN customer community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your suggestion will remain open pending the outcome of the community consultation. Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Greater Flexibility in Advanced Whois-RWS Search</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-12/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 24 Aug 2023 03:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-12/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7 September 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.12 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN allow greater flexibility in Advanced Whois-RWS search results.  ARIN has reviewed this suggestion, and it will be considered for future prioritization as part of a group of Whois-RWS improvements. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;American Registry for Internet Numbers (ARIN)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Multiple Security Keys for 2FA</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-02/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 30 Jan 2023 09:03:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-02/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;07 February 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.2 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN allow multiple hardware security keys for two- factor authentication (2FA) so that a single key cannot be a single point of failure.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree that allowing multiple hardware keys would be beneficial to customers and would increase the robustness of our 2FA implementation. We will investigate the requirements to build this new feature and schedule it for future development. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&#xA;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Limit Length of Members Lines for API</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-01/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 30 Jan 2023 09:02:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-01/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;07 February 2023&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2023.1 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN improve the RSPL output for as-set objects that limited the number of items on single members lines in order to make the output more accurate and useful.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree this change would result in better results for as-set object queries. We will investigate the requirements to build this new feature and schedule it for future development. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improvement to ROA Functionality</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-30/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 08 Dec 2022 09:50:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-30/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12 December 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.30 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN add functionality that allows customers to view the projected change in RPKI validity state of related route announcement(s) before publication when using the Route Object Authorization (ROA) create or delete action in ARIN’s Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Benefits of the RPKI are directly related to the accuracy of data contained in repositories throughout the RPKI ecosystem. Providing ARIN resource holders information they need to make informed decisions when creating/modifying ROAs is a key component to maintaining the accuracy and performance of the RPKI. ARIN agrees that your suggestion to add this feature to our RPKI tools that offers visibility into the impact to announcements of their prefixes prior to the publication of ROAs in the ARIN repository will benefit the entire community. We will add this to our deployment schedule and prioritize it along with other development initiatives. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Phone Numbers Outside of the ARIN Region to be Eligible for SMS Two-Factor Authentication</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-29/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 03 Nov 2022 12:50:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-29/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7 November 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.29 on confirmed receipt, requesting that ARIN enable SMS for two-factor authentication (2FA) for customers who reside outside the ARIN service region.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN will have four options for customers to set up 2FA on their ARIN Online accounts prior to 1 February 2023, when we require accounts to be secured:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Time-based One-time Password (TOTP) using an authenticator of your choice&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Short Message Service SMS or Voice Call for customers &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/sms&#34;&gt;within the ARIN service region&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;FIDO2/Passkey (available January 2023)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We continue to receive input from customers for additional options, and plan to conduct a Community Consultation to assess support for continued development related to 2FA for ARIN Online accounts.  Your suggestion will remain open pending the outcome of the consultation and any potential related development effort.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Functionality to Assist Customers Transitioning From Hosted to Delegated RPKI</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-26/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 17 Oct 2022 12:40:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-26/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 November 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.26 on confirmed receipt, requesting that ARIN add functionality to assist customers transitioning from hosted to delegated RPKI.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree this feature has the potential to ease the transition between RPKI deployment types for organizations with large numbers of resources covered by ROAs.  We will investigate the requirements to build this new feature and schedule it for future development. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Field for Multiple Prefixes on ROA Creation Page</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-23/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 29 Sep 2022 12:45:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-23/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5 October 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.23 on confirmed receipt, requesting that we provide a field to add multiple prefixes at one time for the browser signed ROA creation page. We have development on the roadmap that will simplify the RPKI management of resources, including the handling of ROAs.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Create Beta Test Environment for ASPA and BGPsec Router Keys</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-22/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 29 Sep 2022 12:35:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-22/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 September 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.22 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN add a beta test environment for ASPA and BGP sec router keys.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We rely on customer input to help identify improvements and enhancements to ARIN services and agree this would be a useful feature to allow customers to experiment with these security controls before deploying them in production. We will put this suggestion on the list of features to be considered for future development.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Multiple RPKI Certificate Authorities to Publish to each Org-ID </title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-21/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 28 Jul 2022 12:35:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-21/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 August 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.21 on confirmed receipt, requesting that we allow multiple RPKI Certificate Authorities (CAs) to publish to each Org ID so that organizations can delegate the generation/administration of ROAs to child CAs using ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Repository Service (RPS) for Delegated RPKI.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree with your suggestion that adding this feature would benefit the ARIN community. This enhancement to the ARIN RPS for Delegated RPKI will be added to the development roadmap, pending prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Fellowship Program Application Information</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/apply/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 06 Jul 2022 14:33:57 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/apply/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/images/fellowship_logo.svg&#34; alt=&#34;ARIN Fellowship Program Logo&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Applications for the ARIN 58 Fellowship Program are now open through 19 July 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Know someone who would make a great ARIN Fellow? Encourage them to apply!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can download and share our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/58-Fellowship-Flyer.pdf&#34;&gt;informational flyer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Applications for the ARIN Fellowship Program are now closed. Thank you for your interest.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;!--&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Applications for the ARIN 58 Fellowship Program will open on 6 July 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/beafellow&#34;&gt;Apply Today&lt;/a&gt;  &#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;application-eligibility&#34;&gt;Application Eligibility&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Individuals who are 18 years of age or older and reside in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/region/&#34;&gt;ARIN region&lt;/a&gt; are eligible to apply if they have a demonstrated interest in the American Registry for Internet Numbers, Ltd., (“ARIN”) community and its Policy Development Process for the management of Internet number resources.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>IRR Transaction Log for RESTful API</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-07/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 18 Feb 2022 09:55:32 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-07/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15 March 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.7 on confirmed receipt, requesting that we make a transaction log available for RPSL changes made to the IRR using the REST API, which can be accessed via the API or within the associated account’s web interface. We agree this would be a helpful change and benefit customers using the IRR API. We rely on customer input to help identify improvements and enhancements to ARIN services. Our development calendar is fully booked for 2022, but we will include your suggestion on the list of features for consideration in our 2023 prioritization process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Operational Support for Ghostbusters RPKI records per RFC 6493</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-02/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Jan 2022 12:02:32 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2022/2022-02/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7 March 2022&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2022.2 upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN provider operational support for Ghostbusters RPKI records per RFC 6493. We agree that Support for Ghostbusters records in the ARIN repository gives organizations more control over the contact information they choose to share in the RPKI infrastructure, and we will schedule this for future development.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This suggestion will remain open pending implementation. Thank you for participating in ARIN’s Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improve Usability of Reverse DNS Management in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-20/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 13 Oct 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-20/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15 October 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.20 on confirmed receipt, requesting that we improve the usability of Reverse DNS management in ARIN Online. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Private Comment Field for Customers to ARIN Records</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-19/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Sep 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-19/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;29 September 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.19 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide a Private Comments field for ARIN ASN and NET records that is only visible to ARIN and the organization. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add &#34;Select All on Page&#34; Option for Reverse DNS in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-17/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 17 Sep 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-17/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;23 September 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.17 on confirmed receipt, asking that we add an option to &amp;ldquo;select all on page&amp;rdquo; in Reverse DNS in ARIN Online. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Lock Function to Prevent Org ID from Receiving Reassignments or Reallocations</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-18/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 17 Sep 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-18/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;29 September 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.18 on confirmed receipt, asking that we add a lock function to prevent organizations from receiving reassignments or reallocations. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Read-Only Access to the ARIN API</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-6/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Apr 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-6/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 April 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.6 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide a read-only API key to be used with ARIN’s API. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Support DMARC for ARIN-originated Emails and ARIN Mailing Lists</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-5/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 06 Apr 2021 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-5/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 April 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.5 on confirmed receipt, asking that we support the DMARC protocol for emails sent from ARIN and on the ARIN mailing lists. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Provide Certificate Transparency for RPKI</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 17 Feb 2021 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;23 February 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.3 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide certificate transparency for RPKI. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Remove 256 Record Limitation or Increase Returned Results for Network Queries</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 15 Jan 2021 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2021/2021-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;28 January 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2021.1 upon receipt, requesting that ARIN remove the limitation of 256 results or increase the number of results available when returning the list of network records that are managed by an organization. We are currently reviewing your suggestion and will issue our response as soon as possible.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 February 2021&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This suggestion appears to be a duplicate of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2012/2012-20/&#34;&gt;ACSP Suggestion 2012.20: Remove result limit for Whois-RWS child network queries&lt;/a&gt;, which requests support for allowing queries to return more than 256 network records (the current limitation). That suggestion is awaiting prioritization and has not yet been scheduled on ARIN’s Work Plan. Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Maintain a List of Cybercrime Law Enforcement Offices in ARIN Region</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-18/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2020 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-18/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4 December 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.18 upon response, suggesting that ARIN maintain a list of law enforcement offices in our region that handle cybercrime reports and investigations. ARIN is discussing your suggestion both internally and with our colleagues in law enforcement to determine our next steps.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your participation in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. This suggestion will remain open while ARIN performs additional research and determines a course of action.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Make PPML Archives Searchable</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-15/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-15/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;20 October 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.15 upon receipt, requesting that we provide the ability to search the Public Policy Mailing List (PPML) archives by proposal number, policy number, and proposal subject.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree that this functionality would be valuable and will prioritize it for future implementation. Until this is implemented, you could use the single site search feature in your search engine. For example, to search for policy 2020-1, you could enter the  “site:lists.arin.net ARIN-2020-1” qualifier in Google’s search engine to list various email messages that contain that policy number.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New REST End Point</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-11/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-11/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;07 May 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.11 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide a REST endpoint to download the list of certified prefixes associated with an organization. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Open tickets using Reg-RWS</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-10/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-10/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;29 April 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.10 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide the ability to open tickets with ARIN using the Registration RESTful Service (Reg-RWS) application programming interface (API). We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improvement to &#34;View and Manage Networks&#34; in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-9/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 08 Apr 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-9/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;21 April 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.9 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide the ability to list all records on the View and Manage Your Networks Section and secondary navigation for going back to this page from editing Network Information Actions section. We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RESTful Interface for IRR</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jan 2020 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2020/2020-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11 February 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2020.2 upon confirmed receipt, that we should have a RESTful interface for our new IRR that is compatible with RADb.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As we continue to develop this service, ARIN will strive to ensure compatibility with other Internet Routing Registries (IRRs) but we cannot guarantee compatibility with any one specific IRR. ARIN will develop its restful interface in accordance with current specifications and best practices.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Publish Machine-readable Micro-allocation List</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-24/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2019 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-24/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;17 January 2020&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2019.24 upon confirmed receipt, that ARIN a publish machine-readable micro-allocations list.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Currently the micro-allocations list is generated manually by staff, like many of our other published reports and statistics. We currently have a project in our development backlog to look at ways to automate this reporting on the website.  Because your suggestion aligns well with that effort, it will remain open for consideration as part of an automated reporting project on our future work plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Invoice Improvement</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-21/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 19 Nov 2019 11:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-21/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;09 December 2019&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2019.21 on confirmed receipt, asking that we make our invoice process more compatible with Safari Credit Card Autofill.  We agree this is a beneficial improvement and will prioritize it for future implementation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Download All ROAs for an OrgID</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-20/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 31 Oct 2019 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2019/2019-20/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;08 November 2019&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2019.20 on confirmed receipt, asking that we provide the ability for a customer to download a .csv file that contains all the ROAs associated with their Org ID. We agree that this would be a useful feature for customers and have added this feature to the list of improvements to be included in RPKI service update work that is currently underway.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Contributions: IO/IGO/Governments</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/documents/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 25 Apr 2019 09:31:51 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/documents/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The following are documents contributed by ARIN, or in conjunction with ARIN, to Internet governance-related forums.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;!-- categories are Internet Governance, Law Enforcement &amp; Public Safety, Technical Community, Partnerships &amp; Alliances --&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-secondary panel-table&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped table-bordered table-sortable js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;Internet Governance Contributions&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Title&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Submitted to…&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Date&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/ARIN-CITEL-APR-2026-CCPI-2026-48.pdf&#34;&gt;IPv6 Deployment Information and ARIN Community Programs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CITEL PCC1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;8 April 2026&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/itu_october2025.pdf&#34;&gt;Comments regarding Draft New Recommendation ITU-T Y.2086 (formerly Y.DNI-fr): “Framework and Requirements of Decentralized Trustworthy Network Infrastructure”&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T Study Group 13&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;15 October 2025&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/fcc_august2024.pdf&#34;&gt;Reply Comments on Border Gateway Protocol Risk Mitigation Progress – PS Docket No. 24-146; Reply Comments on Secure Internet Routing – PS Docket No. 22-90&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Federal Communications Commission (FCC), U.S.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;1 August 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/fcc_july2024.pdf&#34;&gt;Comments on Reporting on Border Gateway Protocol Risk Mitigation Progress – PS Docket No. 24-146; Comments on Secure Internet Routing - PS Docket No. 22-90&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Federal Communications Commission (FCC), U.S.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;17 July 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/cisa_july2024.pdf&#34;&gt;Comments on the Proposed Rule for Cyber Incident Reporting for Critical Infrastructure Act of 2022 (CIRCIA) – Docket No. CISA-2022-0010&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, U.S. Department of Homeland Security&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;3 July 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/hoc_january2024.pdf&#34;&gt;Perspectives on the collection, use, and disclosure of Personal Information in Canada&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Standing Committee on Industry and Technology, House of Commons, Canada&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;5 January 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/itud_october2023.pdf&#34;&gt;Considerations in Broadband Deployment – Critical Internet infrastructure, Security, and Support Mechanisms&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-D Study Group 1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;10 October 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/citel_041223.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Informational Contribution&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CITEL PCC1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;12 April 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/NRO_032123.pdf&#34;&gt;NRO Letter to ICANN&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ICANN&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;21 March 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/ITU_280223.pdf&#34;&gt;Comments regarding “Framework and Requirements of Decentralized Trustworthy Network Infrastructure”&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T Study Group 13&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;28 February 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/ARIN_FCC2290_reply_jan2023.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Reply to FCC 22-90 on Secure Internet Routing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Federal Communications Commission (FCC), U.S.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;20 January 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/NRO_mauritius_20220629.pdf&#34;&gt;NRO Letter to Mauritius&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Republic of Mauritius&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;29 June 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/ARIN-reply-to-FCC-22-90-other-filings.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Reply to FCC 22-90 on Secure Internet Routing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Federal Communications Commission (FCC), U.S.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;10 May 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/FINAL_ARIN_response_FCC_22_90.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Response to FCC 22-90 on Secure Internet Routing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Federal Communications Commission (FCC), U.S.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;08 April 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/Final-ARIN-Comments-to-NTIA-WTC-2021-06-07.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Response to Docket No. 210503-0097 RIN 0660-XC050&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NTIA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;07 June 2021&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/Taylor-Secretary-General-CTU-2021-03-04.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN CEO Letter Congratulating New CTU Secretary General&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CTU SG&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;04 March 2021&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/NTIA_WTSA_Response-2020-06-03.pdf&#34;&gt;NTIA&amp;rsquo;s Federal Register Notice WTSA-20 response by ARIN&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NTIA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;03 June 2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/CCPI-2019-34-4761_i.pdf&#34;&gt;Recent Activities at ITU-T Study Groups 2 and 20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CITEL PCC1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;15 April 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/CCPI-2019-34-4760_i.pdf&#34;&gt;IPv6 Deployment Activities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CITEL PCC1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;14 April 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/T17-SG20-C-0569!R1!MSW-E.pdf&#34;&gt;Regarding the draft recommendation &amp;ldquo;Y.IPv6RefModel&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T Study Group 20&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;09 April 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/itu-d-1-221-e-03022019.pdf&#34;&gt;IPv6 case studies from Team ARIN&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-D Study Group 1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;02 March 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/T17-SG20-C-0434!!MSW-E.pdf&#34;&gt;Regarding Draft Recommendation Y.IPv6RefModel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T Study Group 20&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;03 December 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/NTIA_Privacy_rfc2018.pdf&#34;&gt;NTIA’s Notice of Inquiry on International Internet Policy Priorities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NTIA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;25 October 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/relations/governance/ccpi-2018-33-4656_i.pdf&#34;&gt;Evolution of NNAI and Recent Activities at ITU-T SG2 AND SG20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CITEL PCC1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;06 August 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/Response-to-Docket-No.180124068-8068-01-IIPP-NoI.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Contribution to National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) Docket &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NTIA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;17 July 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/T17-TSAG-C-0028!!MSW-E.pdf&#34;&gt;A.25 ambiguity regarding TDs and contributions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T TSAG&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;26 February 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/dr_v6addressing_ituSG20.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Views on Draft Recommendation Y.IPv6RefModel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-T Study Group 20&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;04 September 2017&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/D14-SG01.RGQ-C-0055!!MSW-E.pdf&#34;&gt;Regional Internet Basics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ITU-D Study Group 1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;26 February 2015&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/pdf/ARIN-NTIA-IANA-NOI-Response-Approved-FINAL.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Contributions to Department of Commerce, National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NTIA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;31 March 2011&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Registration Services Agreement (RSA) FAQs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/rsa_faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 12 Sep 2018 15:05:17 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/rsa_faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN provides the FAQs and answers below to enhance the Internet community’s understanding of Registration Services Agreement (RSA) Version 14.0. The FAQs do not alter or otherwise modify any terms of any RSA. For information focused specifically on Legacy Resources, please see our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/legacy/&#34;&gt;Legacy Resources page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-different-about-the-current-arin-registration-services-agreement-rsa&#34;&gt;What is different about the current ARIN Registration Services Agreement (RSA)?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The current RSA (Version 14.0) includes an update to section 13(c). It now allows a customer to terminate the RSA if a change to the Service Terms is believed to materially and adversely impact their rights or use of the Included Number Resources. In such cases, Internet number resources received prior to ARIN’s formation would revert to Legacy Number Resource status, while any resources issued directly by ARIN would be returned.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>WhoWas ReadMe</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/whowas/readme/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Sep 2018 12:09:36 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/whowas/readme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN’s WhoWas report contains historical registration information for a given IP address or Autonomous System Number (ASN). The publication of WhoWas data is provided subject to an approved request under ARIN&amp;rsquo;s WhoWas &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/research/whowas/tou/&#34;&gt;Terms of Use (ToU)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;file-format&#34;&gt;File Format&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Because the WhoWas report contains the entire public history for a given IP address or ASN, it is much larger and more complex than a Whois query response. Each IP address or ASN could have been a part of multiple networks/AS ranges over time and have been issued to multiple organizations, each with its own associated Points of Contact (POCs).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Bulk Whois Readme</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/bulkwhois/readme/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Sep 2018 11:15:22 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/bulkwhois/readme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  This &amp;ldquo;readme&amp;rdquo; file is provided with downloads of Bulk Whois data. Please visit &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/research/bulkwhois/&#34;&gt;Bulk Whois Data&lt;/a&gt; for more information on how to obtain Bulk Whois data, the description of elements, and schema validation instructions.&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The publication of bulk Whois data is provided subject to an approved request under ARIN&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/#bulk-whois&#34;&gt;Bulk Whois Terms of Use (ToU)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Whois data is for Internet operational or technical research purposes pertaining to Internet operations only. It may not be used for advertising, direct marketing, marketing research, or similar purposes. Use of ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Whois data for these activities is explicitly forbidden. ARIN requests to be notified of any such activities or suspicions thereof.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Application Programming Interface (API) Keys</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/api_keys/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 12:14:18 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/api_keys/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;An Application Programming Interface (API) key is a secret code that you can use to identify yourself to ARIN when you interact with us. You create an API key in ARIN Online, and then use the key in interactions with ARIN outside of ARIN Online. Multiple interactions may be performed with the same API key, or you can create multiple API keys to locally track specific requests or to access reports. The API key does not expire, but can be deactivated at any time.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Multifactor Authentication (MFA)</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/multifactor/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 12:14:18 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/multifactor/</guid>
      <description>&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As of 1 February 2023, ARIN requires multifactor authentication (MFA) on all ARIN Online accounts. Users have three methods of multifactor authentication to choose among: an authenticator application, SMS, or a passkey. Please see &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20230201-2fa/&#34;&gt;our announcement&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/2fa/2fafaq/&#34;&gt;FAQ&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 7 October 2024, ARIN will lock all remaining ARIN Online accounts that have not enabled MFA.&lt;/strong&gt; Please see &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20240909/&#34;&gt;our announcement&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;iframe src=&#34;//www.youtube.com/embed/U0qLi-8qXvs&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#34; allowfullscreen title=&#34;Watch at youtu.be/U0qLi-8qXvs&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Multifactor authentication (MFA) is a means of identifying a user through two separate pieces of information or identification. For ARIN Online, these two pieces are your account password and a one-time password generated using a third-party mobile authenticator, provided through SMS, or provided through a passkey. By combining the two proofs of identity that an unauthorized user is unlikely to possess, MFA provides an increased level of security for ARIN Online users.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>DNSSEC Trust Anchors from ARIN</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/dnssec/trust_anchors/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 06 Sep 2018 12:42:15 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/dnssec/trust_anchors/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page at one time contained information on the DNSSEC keys that ARIN used to sign the zones listed below. Since the parent zones for the zones listed below are signed, there is no longer a need to maintain a separate trust anchor file. If you do have one configured, ARIN strongly encourages you to remove it. We will be changing out the trust anchors some time after July 1, 2011.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>About RPKI</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/rpki/info/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Sep 2018 12:58:38 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/rpki/info/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;benefits-of-rpki-adoption&#34;&gt;Benefits of RPKI Adoption&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Adopting Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI) helps establish a more trusted and collaborative environment among Internet number resource holders and network operators connected to the Internet. By adopting RPKI, companies can rely on verifiable information about IP address and route legitimacy, which can help resolve routing issues and combat network attacks. This leads to a more reliable and secure Internet infrastructure for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creating Route Origin Authorizations (ROAs) for your resources benefits more than just you.&lt;/strong&gt; Operators make decisions based on Route Origin Validation, leading to a more reliable and secure Internet infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Hosted RPKI</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/rpki/options/hosted/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Sep 2018 12:58:38 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/rpki/options/hosted/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-hosted-rpki&#34;&gt;What is Hosted RPKI?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hosted Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI) is an infrastructure in which ARIN hosts a Certificate Authority and signs all Route Origin Authorizations (ROAs) for resources within the ARIN region. Only direct resource holders can participate in RPKI. Reallocated and reassigned net resources cannot be added to an organization&amp;rsquo;s RPKI certificate. Any downstream organization must have their upstream provider submit ROAs on their behalf.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hosted RPKI&amp;rsquo;s benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Reg-RWS Quick Start Guide</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/regrws/quickstart/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Sep 2018 09:35:58 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/regrws/quickstart/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN Online users can also use Reg-RWS in addition to the graphical user interface to retrieve and modify records within ARIN&amp;rsquo;s database by sending URLs and XML or Routing Policy Specification Language (RPSL) payloads in an automatable, computer-friendly manner using modern application interfaces that provide strong authentication. You can use Reg-RWS to perform these and other actions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Retrieve and modify information about delegations and networks&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Reassign and reallocate network space&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Retrieve and modify information about Orgs, Points of Contact (POCs), and customers&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Get information about tickets (requests for ARIN to perform an action) and add messages to tickets&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Submit Route Origin Authorizations (ROAs)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Retrieve and edit Internet Routing Registry (IRR) objects&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Request reports, such as WhoWas (historical registration information) or reassignments for a given network&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For more information about Reg-RWS and frequently asked questions, visit &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/regrws/&#34;&gt;Automating Record Management with Reg-RWS&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Whois-RWS API Documentation</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/whois/rws/api/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Aug 2018 10:41:41 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/whois/rws/api/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;background&#34;&gt;Background&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Traditionally, Whois services were offered using the NICNAME/WHOIS protocol as described by RFC 954 and RFC 3912. This protocol is a simple, text-based TCP protocol registered with in the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) for well-known port 43. The specification for the protocol, RFC 3912, did not define either data types or data formats. As a consequence, Whois data varied from service provider to service provider and was far from ideal for programmatic consumption. Consequently, ARIN first provided expanded Whois capabilities in its own ARIN-specific Whois implementation of Whois-RWS.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Submitting a Transfer Pre-approval Request</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/transfers/preapproval/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Aug 2018 14:22:41 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/transfers/preapproval/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN offers transfer pre-approvals to organizations seeking IPv4 address space via a Transfer Between Specified Recipients (&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/#eight3&#34;&gt;NRPM 8.3&lt;/a&gt;) or Inter-RIR Transfers to Specified Recipients (&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/#eight4&#34;&gt;NRPM 8.4&lt;/a&gt;) based on a 24-month projected need. Before requesting a transfer pre-approval, please review ARIN&amp;rsquo;s policies to ensure that you qualify to receive IPv4 addresses. Refer to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/&#34;&gt;ARIN Number Resource Policy Manual (NRPM)&lt;/a&gt; for full details.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; Transfer pre-approval requests will be reviewed based on the organization&amp;rsquo;s projected 24-month need and will not be subject to re-verification for a NRPM 8.3 transfer or a NRPM 8.4 transfer submitted within 24 months of this approval.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Network Modifications</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/manage/netmod/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Aug 2018 11:40:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/manage/netmod/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;You can modify your Network Record (NET) to change the network name, Origin Autonomous System (AS), Resource Point of Contact (POC) handles, and public comments on an IP address block.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; Changes to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/reverse/&#34;&gt;reverse DNS delegation&lt;/a&gt; cannot be made with a network modification.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Network modifications must be submitted by a POC with the appropriate permissions, as defined in the following table:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;POC Types and Permissions&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Action&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Admin&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Tech&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Routing&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modify Network Name&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modify Public Comments&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modify Resource POCs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;using-your-arin-online-account&#34;&gt;Using Your ARIN Online Account&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To modify a NET using ARIN Online:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Referral Whois (RWhois)</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/reassignments/rwhois/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Aug 2018 11:40:32 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/reassignments/rwhois/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-referral-whois-rwhois&#34;&gt;What is Referral Whois (RWhois)?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;RWhois (Referral Whois) is a directory services protocol which extends and enhances the Whois concept in a hierarchical and scalable fashion. It focuses on the distribution of &amp;ldquo;network objects,&amp;rdquo;&amp;ndash;the data representing Internet resources or people&amp;ndash;and uses the inherently hierarchical nature of these network objects (for example, domain names, IP networks, and email addresses) to more accurately discover the requested information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;RWhois synthesizes concepts from other, established Internet protocols to create a more useful way to find resources across the Internet. The RWhois protocol and architecture derive a great deal of structure from the Domain Name System (DNS) [&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1034.txt&#34;&gt;RFC 1034&lt;/a&gt;] and borrow directory service concepts from other directory service efforts, primarily [X.500]. The protocol is also influenced by earlier established Internet protocols, such as the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) [&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc821.txt&#34;&gt;RFC 821&lt;/a&gt;] for response codes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Membership FAQ</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 24 Aug 2018 15:58:33 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;can-i-join-arin-as-an-individual&#34;&gt;Can I join ARIN as an individual?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Membership is on an organization level and is reserved for organizations that hold IPv4 address space, IPv6 address space, and/or Autonomous System Numbers (ASNs) from ARIN under a signed Registration Services Agreement (RSA) with ARIN.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An organization may be an &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/request/individual_request/&#34;&gt;individual business entity&lt;/a&gt;, and as such, the individual would be eligible for membership through their organization.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;does-my-organization-need-to-become-a-member-to-request-resources-from-arin&#34;&gt;Does my organization need to become a member to request resources from ARIN?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your organization does not need to be an ARIN Member to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/request/&#34;&gt;apply for resources&lt;/a&gt; from ARIN or to participate in ARIN&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/pdp/&#34;&gt;Policy Development Process&lt;/a&gt;. Once your organization receives resources from ARIN, you will become a Service Member.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Meetings - Past Sponsors</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/sponsors/past_sponsors/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Aug 2018 14:33:57 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/sponsors/past_sponsors/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN would like to thank all of the companies and organizations that have supported its Public Policy and Members Meetings. With their support, ARIN has been able to stage successful meetings throughout the Internet community it supports.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please see the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/past/&#34;&gt;Past Meetings &amp;amp; Events page&lt;/a&gt; to view full meeting reports.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-style panel-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-header&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h2 class=&#34;card-title&#34;&gt;ARIN 8 (October &amp; November 2021)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-changelog table-sm&#39;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Company/Organization&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Type of Sponsorship&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.lumen.com/&#34; title=&#34;Lumen&#34;&gt;Lumen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Network Sponsor&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://usinternet.com/&#34;&gt;USI&lt;/a&gt; &amp;ldquo;USI&amp;rdquo;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Network Sponsor&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Read Me: Report of Resources with No Valid POCs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/account/records/poc/validation/readme/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Aug 2018 14:43:54 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/account/records/poc/validation/readme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: The schema used in the report of number resources without valid POCs changed with the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/announcements/20170916/&#34;&gt;16 September 2017&lt;/a&gt; update of ARIN Online. This schema is included in the .zip file of the report that is downloaded. Please be sure that your automated scripts parse this new XML format.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The list of number resources without valid POCs is provided subject to an approved request under &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/bulkwhois.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Bulk Whois Acceptable Use Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Whois data is for Internet operational or technical research purposes pertaining to Internet operations only. It may not be used for advertising, direct marketing, marketing research, or similar purposes. Use of ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Whois data for these activities is explicitly forbidden. ARIN requests to be notified of any such activities or suspicions thereof.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Planned Functionality</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/software/planned/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Aug 2018 11:41:30 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/software/planned/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p class=&#34;intro-text&#34;&gt;ARIN&amp;rsquo;s goal is to allow individuals and organizations to manage their ARIN records, requests, and correspondence online. In addition to developing the online account management system, ARIN keeps track of community and internal recommendations for new services and improvements. These items await prioritization, planning, and approval before work can commence. ARIN encourages community input on future upgrades and services. Information gleaned from community feedback, received both online and in person, will be used by ARIN management to help prioritize future work.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Examples: Resource Request Documentation</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/request/documentation/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Aug 2018 10:24:52 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/request/documentation/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As part of the process of requesting number resources from ARIN, there is often a need for the organization making the request to supply documentation to demonstrate how the request meets the specific requirements outlined by policy. To help make this process easier, we provide below several types of documentation that may be required, along with examples you can download. The examples are not intended to demonstrate how to meet specific policy requirements, but to help show the best format for the documentation to be processed as quickly and efficiently as possible.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Your First IPv6 Request</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv6/first_request/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Aug 2018 15:05:41 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv6/first_request/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Are you ready to deploy IPv6, but you&amp;rsquo;re not sure where to begin? Whether you are an end user or an Internet Service Provider (ISP), ARIN can help you determine how much IPv6 address space is appropriate for your organization and tell you how to request space.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;iframe src=&#34;//www.youtube.com/embed/AlSTZY_N_bw&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#34; allowfullscreen title=&#34;Watch at youtu.be/AlSTZY_N_bw&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;i-already-have-ipv4-from-arin-or-its-predecessor-i-need-ipv6&#34;&gt;I already have IPv4 from ARIN (or its predecessor). I need IPv6!&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you have an IPv4 allocation or assignment from ARIN, obtaining IPv6 couldn&amp;rsquo;t be easier.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Request IPv4 Addresses</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/request/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Aug 2018 15:04:38 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/request/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p class=&#34;intro-text&#34;&gt;ARIN experienced depletion of its IPv4 Free Pool on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/announcements/20150924/&#34;&gt;24 September 2015&lt;/a&gt;, however we are still processing and approving customer IPv4 requests. Visit the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/waiting_list/&#34;&gt;Waiting List page&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about how IPv4 requests are being handled.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;intro-text&#34;&gt;You may also consider submitting a &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/transfers/&#34;&gt;transfer request&lt;/a&gt; to acquire IPv4 space.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;reserved-ipv4-address-blocks&#34;&gt;Reserved IPv4 Address Blocks&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since IPv4 depletion, we no longer can fulfill requests for IPv4 addresses unless an organization meets certain policy requirements that reserve blocks of IPv4 addresses for special cases, as outlined below.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Online Improvements for Display of POCs and OrgIDs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-19/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 06 Aug 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-19/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;06 September 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.19 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN Online improvements in the display of orphaned POCs and Org IDs, as well as non-validated POCs.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and note that it is possible to implement as an improvement to ARIN Online. Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We will consider this suggestion, together with other community suggestions requesting enhancements to ARIN Online, for possible inclusion into our 2019 work plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Make Whowas Reports Viewable in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-18/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 03 Aug 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-18/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;06 September 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.18 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make Whowas reports viewable in ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and note that it is possible to implement this as an improvement to the service. Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We will consider this suggestion, together with other community suggestions requesting enhancements to ARIN Online, for possible inclusion into our 2019 work plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>NRO NC Requirements and Responsibilities</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/requirements/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Jul 2018 09:31:21 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/requirements/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;initial-requirements&#34;&gt;Initial Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Incoming NRO NC Members must:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Attend several &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/meetings/&#34;&gt;in-person meetings&lt;/a&gt; held in various locations throughout the year and participate in periodic conference calls.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Sign an &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/nronc_nda.pdf&#34;&gt;ARIN Non-Disclosure Agreement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;responsibilities&#34;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;NRO NC Member responsibilities Include, but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Adhering to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/conflicts/&#34;&gt;Nomination and Appointment Conflict of Interest List&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Attending all regularly-scheduled ARIN, ICANN, and ASO in-person meetings and teleconferences&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Serving as representatives from the ARIN Region on the ICANN Address Supporting Organization Advisory Council (ASOAC), which involves the following responsibilities:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Taking a role in the global policy development process as described in the ASO Memorandum of Understanding&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Providing recommendations to the Board of ICANN concerning the recognition of new RIRs&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Defining procedures for selection of individuals to serve on other ICANN bodies, in particular on the ICANN Board, and implement any roles assigned to the Address Council in such procedures&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Providing advice to the Board of ICANN on Internet number resource policy, in conjunction with the RIRs&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Developing procedures for conducting business in support of their responsibilities, in particular for the appointment of an Address Council Chair and definition of the Chair&amp;rsquo;s responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For additional information on the ASO roles and responsibilities, see the  &lt;a href=&#34;https://aso.icann.org/documents/memorandums-of-understanding/&#34;&gt;ICANN Address Supporting Organization (ASO) MoU&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Current Job Openings at ARIN</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/careers/openings/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Jul 2018 08:14:05 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/careers/openings/</guid>
      <description>&lt;!-- placeholder for when there are no openings --&gt;&#xA;&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;strong&gt;There are no job openings at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-style panel-default&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-header&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h2 class=&#34;card-title&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Employees describe ARIN as offering a supportive, casual, and flexible work environment that provides an atmosphere of continuous learning while being responsive to the community we serve.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Located in Chantilly, Virginia, ARIN offers competitive salaries, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/careers/#benefits&#34;&gt;comprehensive benefits&lt;/a&gt;, training, and education reimbursement. In lieu of stock options (we are a nonprofit, membership association), we have a generous 401(k) retirement plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Committee and Working Group Charters</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/committees/charters/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 15:40:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/committees/charters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;charter-for-the-compensation-committee&#34;&gt;Charter for the Compensation Committee&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/committees/2026_charter_compensationcommittee.pdf&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;(PDF Format)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.0. Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The ARIN Bylaws (including Article VI, Section 3) establishes a Compensation Committee. The Compensation Committee shall only be delegated the powers and authority, if any, from the Board as specified below or in the Bylaws; and for any other work or matters requested by the Board, the Compensation Committee will work to refer any actions or information for consideration by the Board.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meeting Procedures</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/procedures/meetings/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 15:40:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/procedures/meetings/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The following are procedures related to the planning and minuting of meetings of the Board of Trustees, as well as a description of procedures related to the Board, as outlined in the ARIN Bylaws.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;in-person-meetings-approximately-four-annually&#34;&gt;In-Person Meetings (Approximately Four Annually)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;January: Election of officers&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;April: Meetings during the second-quarter Public Policy &amp;amp; Members Meetings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;August: Board Workshop&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;October: Meetings during the fourth-quarter Public Policy &amp;amp; Members Meetings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;teleconferences-five-to-ten-annually&#34;&gt;Teleconferences (Five to Ten Annually)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;May: discussion of 2nd quarter Public Policy &amp;amp; Members Meetings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;November: discussion of 4th quarter Public Policy &amp;amp; Members Meetings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Fourth quarter: finalize ARIN&amp;rsquo;s budget&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Other times as needed: See &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/meetings/&#34;&gt;the Board Agenda and Meeting Minutes page&lt;/a&gt; for the current list of Board minutes. Minutes note whether the meeting was held in-person or via teleconference.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;approval-of-meeting-minutes&#34;&gt;Approval of Meeting Minutes&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN staff, in attendance at each Board meeting, writes a first draft of the meeting minutes and sends them to the Secretary of the Board for preliminary approval. Upon the Secretary&amp;rsquo;s preliminary approval, the draft minutes are sent via email to the ARIN Board of Trustees for a 5 business-day review period. Trustees have those five business days to respond with approval or suggested changes. Lack of response within five days will be construed as preliminary acceptance of the draft minutes. If changes are received, they will be incorporated by the Secretary, and the revised draft will be sent back to the ARIN Board for a final 3 business-day review. The Minutes will be posted as &amp;ldquo;draft&amp;rdquo; on the ARIN website until formal approval by the Board of Trustees, at the next regularly scheduled Board meeting, after which the minutes are posted as approved.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Advisory Council Chair Election Procedures</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/procedures/chair/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 11:27:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/procedures/chair/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Each January, the current members of the Advisory Council must hold an internal election to select its Chair for the calendar year from among the currently seated members of the Advisory Council (&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/&#34;&gt;Bylaws, Article VI, Section 2.b.&lt;/a&gt;). The election process is administered by the Policy Analyst. Note: All current and incoming Advisory Council members will be reminded of the upcoming election process in December prior to the January Advisory Council election.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Bylaws - Appendix A: Change Log</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/changelog/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Jul 2018 11:05:39 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/changelog/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The change log archives the changes made to the ARIN Bylaws; indicates the effective date, and the ARIN Board of Trustees meeting that the change was adopted; identifies the article and section number and provides a description.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;version-32&#34;&gt;Version 32&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/bylaws.pdf&#34;&gt;Archive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effective Date:&lt;/strong&gt; 16 May 2022&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Board of Trustees Meeting Minutes:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/meetings/2022_0516/&#34;&gt;16 May 2022&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-changelog table-sm&#39;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Section&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article V, Section 2, ARIN Meetings&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article V, Sections 3.a, 3.b, 3.c, Membership Rights&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modifications&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 1.b, Board of Trustees, Composition&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification: Board seat expansion&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 1.c, Board of Trustees, Document Requirements&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 1.d, Board of Trustees, Trustee Conflict of Interest&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 1.e, Board of Trustees, Eligibility&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 3.a, Committees, Working Groups and Task Forces, Standing Committees&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification: Adding multiple committees to list&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 3.b, Committees, Working Groups and Task Forces, Special Committees&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 3.c, Committees, Working Groups and Task Forces, Committee Governance&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;New&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 4, Terms of Office&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 4.a, Terms of Office, Limits on Terms of Office&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;New&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Section 7, Interim Appointments and Partial Terms&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VIII, Sections 1.b, 2, 2.a, 2.b, 3.b, Elections and Appointments&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modifications&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Article VI, Sections 2.b, 8; Article VII, Sections 1 - 8; Article IX, Section 6&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Modification (gender-neutral language)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;version-31&#34;&gt;Version 31&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/ARIN_bylaws_v31_15dec21.pdf&#34;&gt;Archive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RPKI-Based BGP Origin Validation</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-13/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Jul 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-13/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 August 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.13 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN enable RPKI-based BGP origin validation in ARIN&amp;rsquo;s own Autonomous Systems and reject &amp;ldquo;invalid&amp;rdquo; route announcements.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and note we would need to implement it with careful consideration given to minimizing impact for customers who may encounter situations that require they query and fix their ROAs managed inside ARIN&amp;rsquo;s hosted RPKI solution in circumstances where they are experiencing their own RPKI-based operational issues. Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We will consider this suggestion, together with other RPKI-related community suggestions, for inclusion into our 2019 work plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/process/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Jul 2018 08:19:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/process/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Contact information provided in a Suggestion submission is for staff use only. Submissions with no contact information will be discarded as invalid. Valid suggestions are &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/&#34;&gt;published and tracked&lt;/a&gt;, public attribution is voluntary.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;version-5-18-january-2018&#34;&gt;Version 5 - 18 January 2018&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/changelog/&#34;&gt;View change log&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/community/acsp/acsp_20180118.pdf&#34;&gt;Printer-friendly version (PDF)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Questions concerning the ACSP itself should be sent to &lt;a href=&#34;mailto:info@arin.net&#34;&gt;info@arin.net&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objective&#34;&gt;Objective&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are occasions when the American Registry for Internet Numbers (ARIN) needs to consult with either the members of ARIN or with the community at large regarding ARIN services and practices. There is also need for a mechanism through which the members and the community are able to suggest changes or additions to ARIN services and practices.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Number Resource Policy Manual Appendix A: Change Log </title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/changelog/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Jul 2018 11:26:37 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/changelog/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The table below contains all archived versions of ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Number Resource Policy Manual (NRPM), including references to implemented policies, Board of Trustees meetings where policies were adopted, impacted sections, and whether these policies were Modifications, Additions, or Removals.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;git-repository&#34;&gt;Git Repository&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Archived NRPM versions are also available as a Git repository at &lt;a href=&#34;https://bitbucket.org/arin-rir/number-resource-policy-manual&#34;&gt;https://bitbucket.org/arin-rir/number-resource-policy-manual&lt;/a&gt; for public read-only access.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The repository contains a single Markdown file with a commit history spanning all NRPM iterations and a user-friendly web interface for viewing differences between versions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Associate Ask ARIN tickets with OrgID</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-10/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Apr 2018 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-10/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 May 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.10 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN allow Org ID association with Ask ARIN tickets.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Ask ARIN tickets are currently support tickets that can be created by individual users through their ARIN Online account. These general support tickets do not currently allow linking to POCs or Org IDs. We understand your suggestion is to allow a web user to open an Ask ARIN support ticket and make it visible to all ARIN Online account holders who are linked under a common Org ID.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow User Default Settings in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-9/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Apr 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-9/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 May 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.9 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN allow user default settings in ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and understand it supplements suggestion 2018.8, but that it also stands alone as a separate suggestion to allow user default settings in areas of ARIN Online that today, or in the future, allow for user settings selection. We further note your call for ARIN to consider separate user-defined settings defaults for separate device types (mobile vs. browser). We will investigate approaches to lists for mobile browsing vs. desktop browsing and attempt to implement common best practices and industry standards in user interface design.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improve List Display in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-8/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 17 Apr 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-8/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 May 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.8 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make improvements to list displays in ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and understand the request is to allow the user to select a full list view in cases where they are presented with pagination. We have also noted the feature request to have your preference saved as an account default.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We are currently reviewing our schedule for changes and new additions through a comprehensive ACSP consultation to determine the suggestion subject areas of highest interest to the community. Following that consultation, we will consider if scheduling for this suggestion may be moved up for 2018 or considered for 2019.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improve POC Validation Functionality</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-7/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Apr 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-7/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 May 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.7 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make improvements to POC validation functionality.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and understand the request would allow an individual associated with a POC under a particular Org ID to be able to validate other POCs associated with that same Org ID, including in situations where the subject individual does not control the other associated POCs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Mass Delete of Managed Reassignments Within ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-4/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 28 Mar 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-4/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 May 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.4 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make it possible to mass delete managed reassignments within ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and note that it is possible to create the functionality you are requesting and believe the new feature would enhance effective management of reassignments within ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We are currently reviewing our schedule for changes and new additions through a comprehensive ACSP consultation to determine the suggestion subject areas of highest interest to the community. Following that consultation, we will consider if scheduling for this suggestion may be moved up for 2018 or considered for 2019.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Automatically Redirect Whois Queries to Secure URL</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 14 Mar 2018 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;28 March 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.3 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN automatically redirect Whois queries to a secure URL.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and understand that you are requesting ARIN automatically redirect user queries of Whois made from “http” to “https”, and that we also consider the use of HSTS for Whois queries. Noting there is interest from the community on this topic, and that a conversation on the arin-consult mailing list has already begun, we will open a formal community consultation for this suggestion. Feedback received during the consultation will help inform how ARIN will proceed in this area.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improvements to Whois Inaccuracy Reporting</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 26 Feb 2018 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2018/2018-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;09 March 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2018.2 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make improvements to Whois inaccuracy reporting.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and agree that ARIN&amp;rsquo;s system for Whois inaccuracy reporting can be improved. Specifically, we intend to convert to a ticketed reporting system. Once this suggestion has been added to our work plan, we will propose an implementation plan to the community through a consultation that includes consideration for the different aspects of your suggestion.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Improvements to POC Searches Within ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-28/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Nov 2017 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-28/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;14 December 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.28 upon confirmed receipt, requesting improvements to POC searches in ARIN Online.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We are currently in the process of making user interface improvements to ARIN Online based on feedback received in previously-submitted suggestions through the ACSP process and other feedback mechanisms. We will include your suggested feedback alongside other suggestions as we continue to make these user interface improvements.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Changes To RegRWS Access With API Key Authentication</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-23/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Nov 2017 09:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-23/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;05 February 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.23 upon confirmed receipt, requesting ARIN make an improvement to our RegRWS service.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have reviewed your suggestion and communicated with you via telephone to better understand your request. We have determined we can accommodate this suggestion, alongside similar API-related suggestions, at a future date when we conduct a comprehensive update to our API. Our development schedule for the 2018 year is currently filled by previously-submitted community suggestions and other system improvements. We will review that schedule for changes and new additions early this year, and at that time will consider if scheduling for this suggestion may be moved up.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow registered brokers to be added to transfer tickets</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-16/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 27 Sep 2017 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-16/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;19 October 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.16 upon confirmed receipt, requesting brokers be allowed to be added to transfer tickets.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As you noted, it is currently possible for organizations to designate transfer brokers as one of their points of contact, thereby allowing them full access to transfer ticket communications between them and ARIN. This is an option available to all organizations who hold direct registrations in the ARIN database, regardless of membership or RSA/LRSA status. Separately, ARIN currently follows instructions from registrants inside their transfer tickets regarding communications with transfer brokers. If a registrant indicates inside their transfer ticket that they authorize ARIN to speak to a particular broker about the status and disposition of their transfer ticket, we follow those instructions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sorting of Allocations / Assignments by org-id in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-13/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 19 Jun 2017 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-13/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;06 July 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN Online does currently allow users to search for their resources by Org ID. Our page design can be improved to better help users know this feature is available. In addition to looking into that improvement, we will also evaluate sort functionality for the &amp;ldquo;view and manage your networks&amp;rdquo; screen when multiple Org IDs are listed. This work will likely be completed in two separate phases, with the first improvement targeted for release during Q4 of 2017.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Changes to IP Address Widget</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-9/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Apr 2017 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-9/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;19 April 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.9 upon confirmed receipt, to make changes to the IP address widget that appears at the top of arin.net to indicate to visitors the IP address they are using to access the site.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree it can be beneficial to users to see improved information about how they are connecting to the ARIN website and that it could act as an additional motivation for IPv6 adoption. We will investigate available implementation options and make this new feature a requirement of our website redesign that begins in Q2 of 2017.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Multiple Primary Billing Contacts</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 11 Feb 2017 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 March 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.3 upon confirmed receipt, to increase the number and type of billing contact options associated with ARIN services for organizations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Having reviewed your suggestion and benefited from an opportunity to talk with you about it, we understand you are looking for ARIN to provide greater flexibility in the area of billing contacts. You described different scenarios to us that may not be satisfied by a single billing contact option. One of those scenarios consisted of an organization who has both a person and a system/machine that would like to receive invoices from ARIN. The person behind the primary billing contact email address would want to receive the initial invoice and all subsequent reminders. The system/machine behind the second billing contact email address may only want to receive the initial invoice, but not the reminders. Because of these different preference profiles described for billing contacts, it is not always an easy solution to simply set up an email alias on the customer side.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Two-factor functionality improvement</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jan 2017 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2017/2017-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 February 2017&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2017.1 upon confirmed receipt, to add functionality to ARIN&amp;rsquo;s current 2-factor authentication implementation. We agree that your suggestion will streamline the use of this service for frequent ARIN Online users and encourage further adoption. We are adding this suggestion to our list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization and expect it to be implemented by Q4 of 2017.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Interactive Fee Calculator</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-12/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Jun 2016 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-12/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;20 July 2016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2016.12 upon confirmed receipt, recommending that ARIN provide an interactive fee calculator enabling resource holders to determine fee impacts based on what-if resources change scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your suggestion appears to have value to the community and therefore we will add it to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/account/features/planned/#engineering-projects-awaiting-prioritization&#34;&gt;Engineering Projects Awaiting Prioritization&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We do not have a schedule for implementation at this time, and we suggest you check for any updates in the software development update report that is given at each of the ARIN meeting. At that time staff will report on software engineering projects have been completed as well as what we anticipate completing in the next six months or so.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title> Improvements to RESTful Web Services</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-11/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 18 Jun 2016 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-11/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;21 June 2016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2016.11 upon confirmed receipt, requesting improvements to our RESTful Web Services. We agree that you should be able to see all the records you have access to for your customers via your API key, and we are adding this to our list of future enhancements found on the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>List All Related Unvalidated POCs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-8/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 May 2016 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-8/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;06 June 2016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2016.8 upon confirmed receipt, related to ARIN&amp;rsquo;s point of contact validation process. We agree that having more validated points of contact is of great value to the community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It is good to hear you are finding the features in our new ARIN Online dashboard useful. As you pointed out, one of the features of the new dashboard includes improved information about point of contact validation for logged in ARIN Online users.In response to your suggestion and other feedback we have received, we will be making additionalimprovements to the point of contact validation process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add PO Field to Invoices in ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-6/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 26 Apr 2016 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2016/2016-6/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 May 2016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2016.6 upon confirmed receipt, to add purchase order numbers to invoices through ARIN Online. We agree adding the PO field to invoices would be helpful to ARIN Online users, and we are adding it to our list of future enhancements found on the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the meanwhile, please note that in most cases, ARIN staff can add the PO number to the invoice upon request. However, staff is unable to make any changes to invoices that have been posted. Please contact &lt;a href=&#34;mailto:billing@arin.net&#34;&gt;billing@arin.net&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Marking ARIN Online Messages as Read</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2015/2015-20/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 23 Dec 2015 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2015/2015-20/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;07 January 2016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree the user experience between POC validation with email responses and the ARIN Online message center can be improved, and we will the feature to the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization found at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment-1&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 April 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This suggestion is not on the 2018 Work Plan and will be considered as part of the Community Consultation on Open ACSPs in April 2018. This consultation will serve as one of the inputs to help determine which suggestions will be included ARIN’s 2019 Work Plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sort Order For Utilization reports from RESTful Whois</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2015/2015-18/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 03 Dec 2015 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2015/2015-18/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 December 2015&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree the sort order on returned IP addresses on a Whois-RWS query can be improved. We plan on adding it to the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization found at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/planned.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for participating in the ARIN Consultation and Suggestion Process. Your suggestion will remain open until implemented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment-1&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 April 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This suggestion is not on the 2018 Work Plan and will be considered as part of the Community Consultation on Open ACSPs in April 2018. This consultation will serve as one of the inputs to help determine which suggestions will be included ARIN’s 2019 Work Plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>POC Validation Message Removal Upon Validation</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-28/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 06 Nov 2013 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-28/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;18 November 2013&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, which was numbered 2013.28 upon receipt. This suggestion is reasonable and we plan on adding it to the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization found at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please note that we will be consulting the ARIN community to help access prioritization of improvements of existing systems, as well as additional services that the community desires. This will be fed back into ARIN&amp;rsquo;s planning process for scheduling development resources to complete the suggestion.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Association of Multiple Networks With A Customer</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-16/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 29 May 2013 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-16/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;17 June 2013&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2013.16 upon confirmation, that ARIN allow multiple &amp;ldquo;network&amp;rdquo; objects to be associated to a single &amp;ldquo;customer&amp;rdquo; object in the Whois-RWS database. Our Chief Engineer wrote about this suggestion topic on the arin-tech-discuss list on 4/30/13 saying:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;When we redesigned our systems to accommodate Reg-RWS we did take into account the ability to have multiple assignments for a customer. While some work is still required on our end to allow this capability, it is not onerous.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title> Enable Use of Extended Characters in Records</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 14 Feb 2013 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2013/2013-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;26 February 2013&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Internationalization is straightforward on the registration side. Unfortunately, internationalization requires special handling on search/retrieval side (directory services). Further, UTF-8 gets complicated when we have legacy directory services that rely on ascii (like the WHOIS protocol). There is an effort underway within the WEIRDS working group of the IETF that is focused on replacing WHOIS with a new protocol with features like internationalization. ARIN, as one of the technology leaders within the WEIRDS WG, will readdress internationalization once IETF has a reasonable standard underway.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Remove result limit for Whois-RWS child network queries</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2012/2012-20/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 24 Oct 2012 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2012/2012-20/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;28 November 2012&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, which was numbered 2012.20 upon receipt. This suggestion is reasonable and we plan on adding it to the list of outstanding projects awaiting prioritization found at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please note that we will be consulting the ARIN community to help access prioritization of improvements of existing systems, as well as additional services that the community desires. This will be fed back into ARIN&amp;rsquo;s planning process for scheduling development resources to complete the suggestion.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Bulk Billing Management</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2012/2012-5/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Apr 2012 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2012/2012-5/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;21 May 2012&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your thoughtful and positive suggestion. We plan on adding it to the list of projects awaiting prioritization:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/features/#tbd&lt;/a&gt;&#xA; &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that the suggestion will remain open.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment-1&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10 April 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This suggestion is not on the 2018 Work Plan and will be considered as part of the Community Consultation on Open ACSPs in April 2018. This consultation will serve as one of the inputs to help determine which suggestions will be included ARIN’s 2019 Work Plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Define access restrictions for APIs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2011/2011-17/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 11 Apr 2011 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2011/2011-17/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12 May 2011&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The initial goal in moving to API Keys was to create a better security framework for ARIN&amp;rsquo;s provisioning system. As we investigate further improvements, we would like to take your suggestion of access control to the community for input. We will be gathering feedback from the community at large about preferences for the setup of simplified access control. It is our intent to schedule a focus time at the next ARIN meeting to discuss various approaches to this issue. The staff will then use that input as a basis for requirements to build access controls into API keys.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meeting of the ARIN Board of Trustees - 15 December 2025</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/meetings/2025_1215/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 23 Dec 2025 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/meetings/2025_1215/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;teleconference&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Teleconference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;attendees&#34;&gt;Attendees&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Nancy Carter, Chair and Treasurer&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Tina Morris, Vice Chair&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Dan Alexander, Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Curran, President &amp;amp; CEO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Ron da Silva, Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Hank Kilmer, Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Robert Seastrom (RS), Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Tacit, Secretary&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;staff&#34;&gt;Staff&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Michael Abejuela, General Counsel&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Erin Alligood, Chief Human Resources Officer&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alyssa Arceneaux, Board Operations Mgr., Scribe&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Richard Jimmerson, COO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Christian Johnson, CISO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Brian Kirk, CFO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Therese Simcox, Sr. Executive Assistant&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Sweeting, CXO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;guest&#34;&gt;Guest&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lee Howard, 2026 Board Trustee (observer)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;regrets&#34;&gt;Regrets&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Peter Harrison, Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Bill Sandiford, Board Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-welcome-agenda-and-conflict-of-interest-disclosure-review&#34;&gt;1. Welcome, Agenda and Conflict of Interest Disclosure Review.&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Chair called the meeting to order at 3:01 p.m. ET noting a couple of Trustee regrets. The Chair then called for any changes to the agenda. The President stated that there was an incident with a customer allocation and he would like the report and any discussed to be added under Any Other Business, and that he would be making a formal request for the incident to be reviewed by the Risk and Cybersecurity Committee.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
