    <item>
      <title>Whois Terms of Use</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/whois/tou/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Apr 2014 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/whois/tou/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effective: 9 April 2014&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please read the following Whois Service Terms of Use (these &amp;ldquo;Terms&amp;rdquo;) carefully because, by accessing and using the Whois database available on ARIN.net (&amp;ldquo;Whois Service&amp;rdquo;), you accept and agree to them. These Terms form an agreement between you and American Registry for Internet Numbers (&amp;ldquo;ARIN&amp;rdquo;).  By using the Whois Service, you represent to us that you are legally competent to enter into this agreement.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These Terms apply to any use of the Whois Service, including compilation, repackaging, dissemination or other use of ARIN Whois data.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Security Certifications</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/certification/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/certification/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/certifications.png&#34; alt=&#34;Security Certifications&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN understands customers’ need to verify appropriate security baselines are being met. To address this, we pursue industry standard security certifications that attest to our ability to safeguard our systems and data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card collapse-card closed&#34; aria-label=&#34;Click for more information about SOC 2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-header collapse-card-blue&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;javascript:void(0)&#34; aria-expanded=&#34;false&#34; aria-controls=&#34;cc-df94aca9c25fb526c3752c9eb724db57&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa fa-chevron-right&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;SOC 2&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34; id=&#34;cc-df94aca9c25fb526c3752c9eb724db57&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Recognizing the global importance of cybersecurity and the value of Service Organization Control (SOC) 2 as a relevant framework to North America and our customer base, ARIN maintains SOC 2 Type II compliance of its Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI). &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/arin_soc3report.pdf&#34;&gt;&amp;raquo;Download our SOC 3 report&lt;/a&gt; (a publicly releasable version of our SOC 2 report)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Board Candidate Code of Conduct: Communications with the ARIN Electorate</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/board_conduct/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 Aug 2025 15:38:54 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/board_conduct/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-general-principles&#34;&gt;1. General Principles&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Candidates for the ARIN Board of Trustees shall conduct their communications with the ARIN electorate in a manner that is professional and respectful. All communications should foster an environment of integrity, transparency, and fairness.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;2-permissible-communications&#34;&gt;2. Permissible Communications&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Candidates may engage with the ARIN electorate to discuss their qualifications, vision, and priorities for the organization. Such communications may include:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Participation in official candidate forums organized by ARIN.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Written statements submitted to ARIN for distribution.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Direct, one-on-one discussions with eligible voters, provided they remain respectful and non-coercive.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Each Candidate shall be allowed to send one message to all of the voting points of contact for member organizations in the ARIN electorate. This message will be sent by ARIN and will cc all candidates to ensure transparency.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;3-prohibited-communications&#34;&gt;3. Prohibited Communications&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Candidates shall not:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Membership Explained</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/explained/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 29 Dec 2021 10:38:33 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/explained/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As specified in ARIN’s Bylaws, there are three types of ARIN Members: Service, General and Trustee. Service and General memberships are associated with an organization, represented within ARIN by a unique Organization Identifier (Org ID). Membership rights for organizations with multiple Org IDs depend on the resources associated under each Org ID.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It is not necessary to become a member of ARIN prior to applying for Internet number resources. Members and non-members alike must justify number resource requests based on utilization criteria. Membership is not required to participate in ARIN&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/pdp/&#34;&gt;Policy Development Process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Voting FAQs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/vote_faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/vote_faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;who-is-eligible-to-vote-in-arin-elections&#34;&gt;Who is eligible to vote in ARIN Elections?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/&#34;&gt;ARIN Member organization&lt;/a&gt; may have one designated &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/voting/&#34;&gt;Voting Contact&lt;/a&gt; to vote in Board of Trustees and Advisory Council elections on their behalf. A Voting Contact must have a valid ARIN Online account to be eligible to vote in elections. Your organization must also be a &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/membership/faq/#what-is-a-general-member-in-good-standing&#34;&gt;General Member in Good Standing&lt;/a&gt; 45 days before a ballot or election.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;will-a-voting-contact-without-an-arin-online-account-be-eligible-to-vote-in-arin-elections&#34;&gt;Will a Voting Contact without an ARIN Online account be eligible to vote in ARIN Elections?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;No. To be eligible to vote, a member organization must designate a Voting Contact with a valid ARIN Online account and be a General Member in Good Standing by the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/&#34;&gt;voter eligibility deadline&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2020 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2020/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Sep 2019 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2020/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;2020-arin-community-grant-program-recipients&#34;&gt;2020 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped table-bordered js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Applications&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Type&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;1 association, 7 corporations, 5 &#34;other&#34; orgs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Region&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;2 Canada, 7 United States, 1 Caribbean, 3 outside ARIN region&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Category (some projects identified multiple categories)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;9 Internet technical improvements, 5 registry processes and technology improvements, 5 Informational outreach, 3 research&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$305,965&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Average funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$23,536&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Projects selected to receive a grant&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding provided (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$60,000&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Project summaries provided by grant recipients.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Past Internet Governance Events</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/past_events/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 12 Sep 2018 09:31:51 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/relations/governance/past_events/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;The links below are for past events and have generally not been updated since they were published. As a result, some content, specifically links to external pages and other references, may be out-of-date or no longer available.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;past-events&#34;&gt;Past Events&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#past-events&#34;&gt;Past Events&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#itu-plenipotentiary-conference-2018-itu_pleni_2018&#34;&gt;ITU Plenipotentiary Conference 2018 {#itu_pleni_2018}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#world-telecommunication-development-conference-2017&#34;&gt;World Telecommunication Development Conference 2017&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#regional-preparatory-meeting&#34;&gt;Regional Preparatory Meeting&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#igf-usa-2016-igf_usa&#34;&gt;IGF USA (2016) {#igf_usa}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#tenth-internet-governance-forum-2015-igf10&#34;&gt;Tenth Internet Governance Forum (2015) {#igf10}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#itu-plenipotentiary-conference-itu_pleni&#34;&gt;ITU Plenipotentiary Conference {#itu_pleni}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#ninth-internet-governance-forum-2014-igf9&#34;&gt;Ninth Internet Governance Forum (2014) {#igf9}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#netmundial---global-multistakeholder-meeting-on-the-future-of-internet-governance-netmundial&#34;&gt;NETmundial - Global Multistakeholder Meeting on the Future of Internet Governance {#netmundial}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#itu-world-telecommunication-development-conference-2014-wtdc_2014&#34;&gt;ITU World Telecommunication Development Conference 2014 {#wtdc_2014}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#eighth-internet-governance-forum-2013-igf8&#34;&gt;Eighth Internet Governance Forum (2013) {#IGF8}&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#no144-moving-to-ipv4-markets-and-legacy-space&#34;&gt;(No.144) Moving to IPv4 Markets and Legacy Space&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#no145-importance-of-regional-coordination-in-internet-governance&#34;&gt;(No.145) Importance of Regional Coordination in Internet Governance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#wtdc-regional-preparatory-meeting-for-the-americas-rpm-ams-wtdc_regional&#34;&gt;WTDC Regional Preparatory Meeting for the Americas [RPM AMS] {#wtdc_regional}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#fifth-world-telecommunication-policy-forum-wtpf-wtpf&#34;&gt;Fifth World Telecommunication Policy Forum (WTPF) {#wtpf}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2013-canadian-internet-forum-cif-regional-event-cif&#34;&gt;2013 Canadian Internet Forum (CIF) [Regional Event] {#cif}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#wsis10-wsis&#34;&gt;WSIS+10 {#wsis}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#world-conference-on-international-telecommunications-wcit-wcit2012&#34;&gt;World Conference on International Telecommunications (WCIT) {#wcit2012}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#world-telecommunication-standardization-assembly-wtsa-wtsa2012&#34;&gt;World Telecommunication Standardization Assembly (WTSA) {#wtsa2012}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;itu_pleni_2018&#34;&gt;ITU Plenipotentiary Conference 2018&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dubai, UAE; 29 October - 16 November 2018&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;hover-tip&#34; data-bs-toggle=&#34;tooltip&#34; title=&#34;This content has expired or been removed.&#34; data-bs-custom-class=&#34;deadlink&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;javascript:void(0)&#34; data-link=&#34;https://www.itu.int/web/pp-18/en/&#34;&gt;More information…&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Micro-allocations</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/microallocations/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:38:52 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/microallocations/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The policy regarding micro-allocations is contained in Sections &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/#4-4-micro-allocation&#34;&gt;4.4&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/nrpm/#6-10-micro-allocations&#34;&gt;6.10&lt;/a&gt; of the Number Resource Policy Manual. Micro-allocations are made from specific blocks reserved for micro-allocation purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;micro-allocations-for-internal-infrastructure&#34;&gt;Micro-allocations for Internal Infrastructure&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IPv6 micro-allocations for internal infrastructure are made from 2001:0506::/31.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0002::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0008::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0010::/45&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0028::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0033::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0038::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:0100::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:1000::/36&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:2000::/36&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;2001:0506:003A::/48&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;micro-allocations-for-exchange-points&#34;&gt;Micro-allocations for Exchange Points&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The following blocks of IP addresses have been allocated to organizations under ARIN&amp;rsquo;s Micro-allocation Policy for exchange points. In IPv4, ARIN makes these allocations from 149.112.0.0/16 and 206.0.0.0/8. In IPv6, ARIN makes these allocations from 2001:0504::/31.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>IPv4 Private Address Space and Filtering</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/address_filters/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:38:52 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/address_filters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;According to standards set forth in Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) document &lt;a href=&#34;http://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1918&#34;&gt;RFC-1918&lt;/a&gt;, the following IPv4 address ranges are reserved by the IANA for private internets, and are &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; publicly routable on the global internet:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10.0.0.0/8 IP addresses:&lt;/strong&gt; 10.0.0.0 &amp;ndash; 10.255.255.255&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;172.16.0.0/12 IP addresses:&lt;/strong&gt; 172.16.0.0 &amp;ndash; 172.31.255.255&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;192.168.0.0/16 IP addresses:&lt;/strong&gt; 192.168.0.0 – 192.168.255.255&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that only a &lt;em&gt;portion&lt;/em&gt; of the &amp;ldquo;172&amp;rdquo; and the &amp;ldquo;192&amp;rdquo; address ranges are designated for private use. The remaining addresses are considered &amp;ldquo;public,&amp;rdquo; and thus are routable on the global Internet.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Current and Past ARIN Fellows</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/past_fellows/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Aug 2018 14:33:57 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/past_fellows/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/images/fellowship_logo.svg&#34; alt=&#34;ARIN Fellowship Program Logo&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;p class=&#34;intro-text&#34;&gt;Congratulations to Current and Past ARIN Fellows&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-57&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ARIN57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Louisville, Kentucky&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;April 2026&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;fellow-list&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col-12 col-sm-4&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jasmine Cha&lt;/strong&gt;, RISE Program Coordinator, Apathy is Boring; Graduate Student, University of the People&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zulqar Nayen&lt;/strong&gt;, Principal Instructional Designer, Independent Consultancy&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Canada)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col-12 col-sm-4&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Henrik Van Tassell&lt;/strong&gt;, Student, University of Vermont&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;James Lord&lt;/strong&gt;, Network Administrator and Network Architect, Intlos&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Justin Gehrke&lt;/strong&gt;, Vulnerability and Threat Program Manager, Rush University Medical Center&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michael Torres&lt;/strong&gt;, Senior Network Engineer, Blue Stream Fiber&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navin Suvarna&lt;/strong&gt;, Principal Architect, Cisco&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robert Jones&lt;/strong&gt;, Network Engineer, Adams Fiber&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tyler Forajter&lt;/strong&gt;, Cybersecurity Engineer, Community Health Network&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weitong Li&lt;/strong&gt;, Researcher, Virginia Tech&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(U.S. &amp; Outlying Areas)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Expected Qualifications and Responsibilities</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/requirements/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 15:40:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/requirements/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11 June 2025&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;p class=&#34;intro-text&#34;&gt;Service on ARIN’s Board of Trustees requires an understanding of ARIN’s role and its relevance to the ongoing smooth functioning of the Internet.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-style panel-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-header&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h2 class=&#34;card-title&#34;&gt;Relevant Documents&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/procedures/conduct/&#34;&gt;Volunteer Code of Conduct&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/procedures/nda.pdf&#34;&gt;Nondisclosure Agreement Form&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/procedures/coi.pdf&#34;&gt;Confict of Interest Affidavit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/bot_qualifications.pdf&#34;&gt;Print Version of this document&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;primary-duties-and-responsibilities&#34;&gt;Primary Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As a member of the ARIN Board of Trustees, responsible for the following:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Guide ARIN’s strategic direction and Mission&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Oversee ARIN’s Policy Development Process and ensure that policies developed adhere to the process&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Be accountable to the ARIN membership&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Approve objectives and evaluate the performance of the President &amp;amp; CEO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Develop and approve ARIN’s strategic plan, operating plan, and annual budget&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Oversee ARIN’s operating and fiscal performance&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Regularly attend and participate in Board meetings and committee meetings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Serving as a Trustee is a significant time commitment. Trustee workload varies from year to year; however, an overview of time required is as follows:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Former Members of the ARIN Advisory Council</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/former/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 11:27:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/former/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN would like to acknowledge the guidance and expertise provided by the former members of the Advisory Council. Listed below are the names of the former members and the dates of their terms.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;Former Council Members&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Dates of Service&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kendrick Knowles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2023 - December 2025&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Matthew Gamble&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2024 - December 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daniel Schatte&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2024 - December 2024&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Andrew Dul&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;March 2003 - December 2005; January 2014 - December 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anita Nikolich&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2020 - December 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Amy Potter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2016 - December 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chris Tacit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2015 - December 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joe Provo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2017 - December 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alyssa Quinn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2017 - December 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kerrie Richards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2017 - December 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rob Seastrom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2004 - December 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gary Giesen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January - December 2021&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owen DeLong&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2007 - June 2021&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tina Morris&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2014 - December 2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chris Woodfield&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2018 - December 2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;David Farmer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2008 - December 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Springer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2012 - December 2018&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dan Alexander&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2006 - December 2017&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;David Huberman&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2015 - November 2017&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cathy Aronson&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;June 1998 - December 2016&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scott Leibrand&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2008 - December 2016&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Milton Mueller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2013 - December 2016&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kevin Blumberg&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2012 - August 2016&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Heather Schiller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;October 2006 - December 2015&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bill Darte&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;December 1997 - December 2014&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Sweeting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2009 - December 2014&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stacy Hughes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - May 2014&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bill Sandiford&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2009 - December 2013&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chris Grundemann&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2011 - December 2013&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chris Morrow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2010 - December 2012&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Martin Hannigan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2011 - October 2012&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marc Crandall&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2009 - December 2011&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marla Azinger&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2005 - December 2010&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tom Zeller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;November 2009 - December 2010&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lea Roberts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2000 - December 2009&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leo Bicknell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2004 - December 2009&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul Andersen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2004 - December 2009&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Suzanne Woolf&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2003 - December 2008&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alec Peterson&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 2008&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Matt Pounsett&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2006 - December 2008&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alex Rubenstein&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2005 - December 2007&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ron da Silva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - December 2007&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark Kosters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2000 - December 2006&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Sweeting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2000 - December 2005&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sanford H. George&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - December 2004&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kevin Martin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2001 - December 2004&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dale Finkelson&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;April 2003 - December 2003&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dana Argiro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2003 - December 2003&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tanya Hinman&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2003 - February 2003&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dawn Martin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - March 2003&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;lyric apted&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - November 2002&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Brown&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - November 2002&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Barbara Roseman&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2001 - December 2002&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steve Corbato&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1999 - December 2001&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tony Li&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1999 - December 2001&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bill Manning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1999 - December 2001&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Justin Newton&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1999 - December 2001&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jessica Porter**&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - August 2002&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guy Middleton&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 2001&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hilarie Orman&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 2000&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;David Whipple&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 2000&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michael Dillon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - April 2000&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avi Freedman&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2001 - December 2003; January 1998 - December 1999&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ed Kern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1999&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hank Kilmer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1999&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michael DeShazo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1998&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Doug Humphrey&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - 3 March 1998*&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Klensin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1998&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Samir Saad&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1998&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Karl Denninger&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - September 1998&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;* Elected to the ARIN Board of Trustees on this date&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Customer Security Resources</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/resources/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/resources/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/security/resources.png&#34; alt=&#34;Security Practices&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Although ARIN has implemented many security measures, we need your help in ensuring these methods keep your data safe. See below for some of the ways you can help protect your resources.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Click on each link to expand/for more information&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;required&#34;&gt;Required&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card collapse-card closed&#34; aria-label=&#34;Click for more information about Multifactor Authentication (MFA)&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-header collapse-card-blue&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;javascript:void(0)&#34; aria-expanded=&#34;false&#34; aria-controls=&#34;cc-e0c218ffbc192e8cd829ed2c762363b6&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa fa-chevron-right&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Multifactor Authentication (MFA)&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34; id=&#34;cc-e0c218ffbc192e8cd829ed2c762363b6&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Multifactor authentication (MFA) is a means of identifying a user through two separate pieces of information or identification. By combining the two proofs of identity that an unauthorized user is unlikely to possess, MFA provides an increased level of security for ARIN Online users. MFA is required on all ARIN Online accounts. &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/security/multifactor/&#34;&gt;&amp;raquo;Learn more&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Updating Internet Coordination Policy-2</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/icp2/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 10 Apr 2025 09:31:21 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/nronc/icp2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;col&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-style panel-default&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-header&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h2 class=&#34;card-title&#34;&gt;ARIN Second ICP-2 Webinar On Demand&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Register to watch ARIN&amp;rsquo;s NRO NC representatives present an overview of the ICP-2 Review background, purpose, principles, and timeline along with discussion of the second proposed draft. &lt;!--Community participation is critical to the success of this process, so join us for this valuable opportunity to learn more and share your feedback on the draft RIR Governance Document.--&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://arin.zoom.us/rec/share/HePAP60NVm0JOd3UysIKZSVu1vmgrPBMKwoxPxMEl_mRjj7qw7ugnn0VyYXu3Fct.moW81SXLmdHNOGuW&#34;&gt;View ARIN’s Second ICP-2 Webinar&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2019 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2019/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Sep 2019 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/recipients/2019/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;2019-arin-community-grant-program-recipients&#34;&gt;2019 ARIN Community Grant Program Recipients&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped table-bordered js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Applications&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;23&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Type&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;3 associations, 10 corporations, 1 LLC, 9 &#34;other&#34; orgs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Organization Region&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;2 Canada, 16 United States, 0 Caribbean, 5 outside ARIN region&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Category (some projects identified multiple categories)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;11 Internet technical improvements, 3 registry processes and technology improvements, 16 informational outreach&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$350,651&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Average funding requested (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$15,246&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Projects selected to receive a grant&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tr class=&#34;table-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th scope=&#34;row&#34;&gt;Total funding provided (USD)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;$44,500&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Project summaries provided by grant recipients.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Extended Delegation Statistics</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/nro_stats/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:39:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/nro_stats/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN publishes extended delegation statistics files in accordance with the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net&#34;&gt;Number Resource Organization&amp;rsquo;s (NRO)&lt;/a&gt; standardized format for each Regional Internet Registry to report the status of Internet number resources within their regions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The delegated-extended file contains a daily updated report of the distribution of Internet number resources:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;IPv4 address ranges&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;IPv6 address ranges&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Autonomous System Numbers (ASNs)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; This report does not include reallocation or reassignment data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;file-availability&#34;&gt;File Availability&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Extended statistics files (filenames containing &amp;ldquo;delegated-arin-extended-YYYYMMDD&amp;rdquo;) are available for use via HTTPS at &lt;a href=&#34;https://ftp.arin.net/pub/stats/arin/&#34;&gt;https://ftp.arin.net/pub/stats/arin/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Nomination Committee FAQs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/nomcom_faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Aug 2018 13:38:54 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/processes/nomcom_faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;!--&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;There are a number of significant changes affecting the 2022 ARIN Elections - &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/blog/2022/06/15/changes-to-elections-2022/&#34;&gt;check out our summary&lt;/a&gt; with links to detailed explanations!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;--&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-the-purpose-of-the-nominating-committee&#34;&gt;What is the purpose of the Nominating Committee?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Nominating Committee (The NomCom) is responsible for recruiting nominees for the ARIN Board of Trustees (Board), Advisory Council (AC), and Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC) in accordance with the Bylaws and the Election Processes. (&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/bylaws/#a-nomination-committee&#34;&gt;Bylaws, Article VIII, Section 2.a.&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Former Trustees</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/former/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Jul 2018 15:40:12 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/former/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN would like to acknowledge the guidance and leadership provided by the former members of our Board of Trustees. Listed below are the names of former members and the dates of their terms.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;Former Board Members and Dates of Service&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Dates of Service (and offices held, if any)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Bill Sandiford&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2014 - December 2025&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chair: January 2022- October 2025&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Bram Abramsom&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2021 - February 2023&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Catherine Middleton&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2020 - December 2022&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Paul Andersen&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2009 - December 2021&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: January 2011- December 2012&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vice Chair: January 2013- December 2016&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chair: January 2017- December 2021&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Dan Alexander&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2018 - December 2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Patrick Gilmore&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2017 - December 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Regenie Fräser&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2019 - December 2019&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Aaron Hughes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2013 - December 2018&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vice Chair: January - May 2017&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Bill Woodcock&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2003 - December 2017&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vice Chair: May - December 2017&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Merike Kaeo&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2017 - December 2017&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Timothy Denton&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2009 - August 2017&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chair: January 2011 - January 2014&lt;br&gt;Secretary: January 2014 - August 2017&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Vinton G. Cerf&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2011 - December 2016&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chair: January 2014 - June 2016&lt;br&gt;Vice Chair: July 2016 - December 2016&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Paul Vixie&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2005 - December 2013&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chair: April 2009 - January 2011&lt;br&gt;Secretary: January 2011 - December 2013&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Scott Bradner&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;August 1997 - December 2012 &lt;em&gt;(Founding Member)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Secretary: August 1997 - February 2009&lt;br&gt;Treasurer: February 2009 - January 2011&lt;br&gt;Vice Chair: January 2011 - December 2012&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Lee Howard&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2006 - December 2010&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: January 2006 - February 2009&lt;br&gt;Secretary: February 2009 - December 2010&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;January 2002 - December 2004&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: January 2002 - December 2004&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Bill Manning&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2002 - November 2008&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Ray Plzak&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;September 2000 - November 2008&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;ARIN President&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;David Conrad&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2000 - October 2005&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: January - December 2005&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Scott Marcus&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 2000 - May 2002&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Michael Straty&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1999 - December 2001&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: January 2000 - December 2001&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Doug Humphrey&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;March 1998 - December 1999&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Ken Fockler&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;January 1998 - December 1998&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: March 1998 - December 1999&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Kim Hubbard&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;August 1997 - August 2000 &lt;em&gt;(Founding Member)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;ARIN President&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Don Telage&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;August 1997 - December 1999 &lt;em&gt;(Founding Member)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Randy Bush&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;August 1997 - March 1998 &lt;em&gt;(Founding Member)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Treasurer: August 1997 - March 1998&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Raymundo Vega Aguilar&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;August 1997 - December 1997 &lt;em&gt;(Founding Member)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/jon/&#34;&gt;Jon Postel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Former Ex-officio Member of the Board of Trustees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Resources Under Registration Services Agreement (RSA) Report</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/resources/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 02 Oct 2023 13:39:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/resources/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To help research and education organizations analyze Internet routing security, ARIN publishes a daily report every morning that lists each organization and whether they receive our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/legacy/services/&#34;&gt;full suite of registry services or our basic legacy services&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To deploy ARIN&amp;rsquo;s routing security services, an organization must be covered under a &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/#registration-services-agreement&#34;&gt;Registration Services Agreement&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/#legacy-registration-services-agreement&#34;&gt;Legacy Registration Services Agreement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The zip file is in CSV format, and will contain two files: one for networks and one for Autonomous System Numbers (ASNs). Each report will list the Org name, Org handle, Network or AS handle, IP address range or ASN, and what tier of services they qualify to receive from ARIN.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RIR Statistics</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/rir/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:39:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/rir/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The following reports are produced as part of a joint Regional Internet Registry (RIR) project to provide consistent and accessible Internet number resource statistics to the global Internet community to facilitate research on and analysis of the global use of Internet number resources. Some of these reports are updated daily by each RIR, and collective statistics are gathered and published on a regular basis.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;collective-statistics&#34;&gt;Collective Statistics&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net/about/rirs/statistics/&#34;&gt;NRO Internet Number Resource Status Report&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;rir-statistical-reports&#34;&gt;RIR Statistical Reports&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://stats.afrinic.net/&#34;&gt;AFRINIC Statistics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://stats.apnic.net/&#34;&gt;APNIC Statistics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.lacnic.net/en/web/lacnic/estadisticas-asignacion&#34;&gt;LACNIC Statistics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.ripe.net/analyse/&#34;&gt;RIPE NCC Statistics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;raw-historical-delegation-information&#34;&gt;Raw Historical Delegation Information&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;ftp://ftp.afrinic.net/pub/stats/afrinic/&#34;&gt;AFRINIC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;ftp://ftp.apnic.net/pub/apnic/stats/apnic/&#34;&gt;APNIC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://ftp.arin.net/pub/stats/arin/&#34;&gt;ARIN&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;ftp://ftp.lacnic.net/pub/stats/lacnic/&#34;&gt;LACNIC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;ftp://ftp.ripe.net/ripe/stats/&#34;&gt;RIPE NCC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Election Archives</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/archive/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Aug 2018 13:38:54 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/oversight/elections/archive/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Below you will find links relating to archival ARIN election information, including annual elections of the Board of Trustees, Advisory Council (AC), and the NRO NC / ASO AC.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;2025&#34;&gt;2025&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Slate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/board_nomcom_guidance2025.pdf&#34;&gt;Board Guidance to the 2025 NomCom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20250916-candidateslate/&#34;&gt;16 September 2025 - Announcement&lt;/a&gt;  &lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/2025_voter_guide.pdf&#34;&gt;Candidate Biographies&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statements of Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;!--[Archive](https://arin-elections.net)--&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/2025_sos/&#34;&gt;Archive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20251110-results/&#34;&gt;10 November 2025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/2025-eligible-voters.csv&#34;&gt;2025 Eligible Voter List  &lt;/a&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/2025-subregion-voters.xlsx&#34;&gt;2025 Voters by Subregion&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;2024&#34;&gt;2024&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Slate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/board_nomcom_guidance2024.pdf&#34;&gt;Board Guidance to the 2024 NomCom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20240910-candidateslate/&#34;&gt;10 September 2024 - Announcement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20241001/&#34;&gt;01 October 2024 - Amended Announcement&lt;/a&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/participate/oversight/elections/2024_voter_guide.pdf&#34;&gt;Candidate Biographies&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
