      <description>&lt;style&gt;&#xA;table th:first-of-type {&#xA;    width: 20%;&#xA;}&#xA;table th:nth-of-type(2) {&#xA;    width: 20%;&#xA;}&#xA;table th:nth-of-type(3) {&#xA;    width: 20%;&#xA;}&#xA;table th:nth-of-type(4) {&#xA;    width: 40%;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-secondary panel-table&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;table class=&#39;table table-striped table-bordered js-data-responsive&#39;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;2026 Board of Trustees Travel Log&lt;/caption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Event&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Date&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Location&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th scope=&#39;col&#39;&gt;Attendee(s)&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Board of Trustees Face-to-Face Meeting&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;13-14 January&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Miami Beach, FL&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Dan Alexander, Nancy Carter, Peter Harrison, Lee Howard, Hank Kilmer, Tina Morris, Rob Seastrom, Ron da Silva, Chris Tacit&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Advisory Council Face-to-Face Meeting&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;30 January&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;San Francisco, CA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Nancy Carter, Rob Seastrom&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NANOG 96&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;2-4 February&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;San Francisco, CA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Hank Kilmer, Rob Seastrom&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;APNIC 61&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;9-11 February&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Jakarta, Indonesia&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Nancy Carter, Ron da Silva&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Number Resource Organization Executive Council (NRO EC) Face-to-Face&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;13-14 February&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Jakarta, Indonesia&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Nancy Carter&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ICANN 85&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;7-12 March&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Mumbai, India&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Peter Harrison, Chris Tacit&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;19-22 April&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Louisville, KY&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Dan Alexander, Nancy Carter, Peter Harrison, Lee Howard, Hank Kilmer, Tina Morris, Rob Seastrom, Ron da Silva, Chris Tacit&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;NACD Leading Minds&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;7 May&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Denver, CO&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Ron da Silva&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;RIPE 92&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;18-22 May&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Edinburgh, Scotland&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Tina Morris, Hank Kilmer, Lee Howard&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;LACNIC 45&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;25-28 May&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Panama City, Panama&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Lee Howard&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;ICANN 86&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;8-11 June&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Seville, Spain&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Dan Alexander, Nancy Carter, Tina Morris&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;AIS 26/AFRINIC 37&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;22-26 June&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Nairobi, Kenya&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Ron da Silva&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;travel-schedules-for-previous-years&#34;&gt;Travel Schedules for Previous Years&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2025/&#34;&gt;2025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2024/&#34;&gt;2024&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2023/&#34;&gt;2023&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2022/&#34;&gt;2022&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2021/&#34;&gt;2021&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/welcome/board/travel_schedule2020/&#34;&gt;2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/welcome/board/2019_bot_travel/&#34;&gt;2019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/welcome/board/2018_bot_travel/&#34;&gt;2018&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Implementation Notes for ARIN&#39;s Web-Based IRR</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/irr/irr-online-implementation/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2020 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/irr/irr-online-implementation/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The following updates have been made to this document since its original publication:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Updated 9 June 2020 to provide FTP and &lt;a href=&#34;#nrtm&#34;&gt;NRTM&lt;/a&gt; information for for post-deployment configuration.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Updated 1 February 2021 to provide information about the IRR RESTful API.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Updated 3 June 2021 because records created in IRR-online can now be viewed, edited, and changed with RESTFul commands.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Updated January 17 2025 preceding the retirement of ARIN&amp;rsquo;s FTP server.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN’s web-based IRR (IRR-online) is scheduled be deployed on Wednesday, 10 June 2020. This system provides improvements and capabilities beyond the email template-based system (referred to as ARIN-email). Access to the IRR-online system will be available from the navigation menu in ARIN Online, and will provide IRR integration with your ARIN Online resources.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>NRO Transfer Log Format</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/transferlog_format/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:39:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/transferlog_format/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;transfer-log-information&#34;&gt;Transfer Log Information&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Transfer log files can be obtained &lt;a href=&#34;https://ftp.arin.net/pub/stats/arin/transfers&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; with the most current being available &lt;a href=&#34;https://ftp.arin.net/pub/stats/arin/transfers/transfers_latest.json&#34;&gt;via JSON format&lt;/a&gt;. Examples for the files are provided and specifications are provided below.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Transfer log information is also available via the &lt;a href=&#34;https://account.arin.net/public/transferLog.xhtml&#34;&gt;Statistics: Specified Transfers of Internet Number Resources&lt;/a&gt; page.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;nro-transfer-log-format&#34;&gt;NRO Transfer Log Format&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The NRO transfer log is a common format to publish IP address and Autonomous System transfers within RIRs and between RIRs. The format of this log accommodates the description of transfers by both an RIR and the aggregate of transfers from all RIRs by the NRO.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Service Level Reports</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/slr/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Sep 2018 13:39:26 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/research/statistics/slr/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN periodically reports service level commitments and performance against those commitments for community provided services. These reports detail the stated service level commitments and associated performance by department and service. Service Level Reports are included in the Annual Report.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;annual-service-level-reports&#34;&gt;Annual Service Level Reports&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/annual/reports/2022_annualreport.pdf&#34;&gt;2022&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/annual/reports/2021_annualreport.pdf&#34;&gt;2021&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2020.pdf#page=15&#34;&gt;2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2019.pdf#page=10&#34;&gt;2019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2018.pdf#page=10&#34;&gt;2018&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2017.pdf#page=10&#34;&gt;2017&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2016.pdf#page=10&#34;&gt;2016&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/about/corporate/annual/reports/report2015.pdf#page=10&#34;&gt;2015&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2014/&#34;&gt;2014&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2013/&#34;&gt;2013&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2012/&#34;&gt;2012&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2011/&#34;&gt;2011&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2010/&#34;&gt;2010&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/vault/reference/research/statistics/slr_2009/&#34;&gt;2009&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Internet Routing Registry FAQ</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/irr/irr_faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 07 Dec 2020 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/irr/irr_faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;infobox&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: As of 4 April 2022, the ARIN-NONAUTH database has been retired, and the email template entry method is no longer available. &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20220404-irr/&#34;&gt;Please see our announcement&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;my-isp-said-i-have-to-publish-information-in-an-irr-what-does-that-mean&#34;&gt;My ISP said I have to publish information in an IRR. What does that mean?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An IRR (Internet Routing Registry) record tells ISPs how you authorize your resources to be used. ARIN maintains an IRR that allows registrants of AS numbers and IP addresses to publish that information so that ISPs can make appropriate routing decisions. This helps ensure ISPs will recognize your routes as legitimate and enables them to ignore unauthorized routes published by someone else.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Responsible Disclosure Policy</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/disclosure/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/reference/materials/trust/disclosure/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is committed to keep our systems and data secure. This policy is intended to give security researchers clear guidelines for which systems and types of research are covered under this policy, to convey our preferences in how to submit discovered vulnerabilities to us, and how long we ask security researchers to wait before publicly disclosing vulnerabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our responsible disclosure policy is not an invitation to actively hack and potentially disrupt our company network and online services. Activity conducted outside the guidelines described in this policy is not authorized, and ARIN will not extend the protections described in the Authorization section below to such activity.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Deadline Approaching — Make Sure Your Organization is Eligible to Vote in ARIN’s Upcoming Elections!</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260810/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260810/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To vote in this year’s ARIN Elections, organizations must be classified as a General Member in Good Standing as of 5:00 PM ET on Monday, 7 September 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An organization is considered in good standing if it is current on all annual fees and has a valid Voting Contact on record. If you are currently associated with an ARIN General Member, please ensure your organization has no overdue invoices and that a Voting Contact is designated in your account before 7 September.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The State of IPv6 in the Caribbean</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/08/07/state-ipv6-caribbean-2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/08/07/state-ipv6-caribbean-2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As ARIN prepares to participate in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/events/CANTO41/&#34;&gt;41st Caribbean Association of National Telecommunications Organizations Conference &amp;amp; Trade Exhibition&lt;/a&gt;, CANTO 2026, we return to our annual review of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ipv6&#34;&gt;IPv6&lt;/a&gt; progress across the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/caribbean&#34;&gt;Caribbean&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The 2026 results point to broader regional movement. Measured IPv6-capable traffic increased in 24 of the 31 countries and territories included in the review. Based on the jurisdictions represented in this year’s table, the unweighted regional average rose from 20.02 percent in 2025 to 24.66 percent in 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Your Number Resource Record Is a Part of the Internet&#39;s Infrastructure — Respect It Like One</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/08/05/legacy-whois-stewardship/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 08:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/08/05/legacy-whois-stewardship/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As a Regional Internet Registry, ARIN issues Internet number resources to meet operational needs. Our database is a publicly searchable record of the registration data we maintain for every resource issued in our region. That includes &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/legacy/&#34;&gt;legacy resources&lt;/a&gt; — the ones that predate ARIN&amp;rsquo;s founding.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The published data referencing legacy resources is still doing real work to facilitate how the Internet routes traffic, investigates abuse, and holds networks accountable. It is this data that ensures the uniqueness of the resources, and keeping it up to date is the responsibility of the organization holding those resources.  Outdated information creates more potential for abuse and other problems than you might expect.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/jacksonville/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/jacksonville/</guid>
