    <item>
      <title>ARIN on the Road is heading to Jacksonville, Florida!</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260804/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260804/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is committed to helping organizations get the most value out of their customer experience, which is why we provide in-person updates and support via our ARIN on the Road traveling workshop.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Have questions about IPv6 resources? Wondering how your organization can deploy Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI)? Need help navigating ARIN Online? Get your questions answered at our September ARIN on the Road event in Jacksonville, Florida.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/jacksonville&#34;&gt;Register for ARIN on the Road Jacksonville&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN-prop-353: Define Out Of Region Use</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_353/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_353/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-statement&#34;&gt;Problem Statement&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Section 9, Out Of Region Use, sets requirements for this use case and the treatment of space used as such for future justifications, but does not include a definition of the term. As such, there have been recurring concerns from the community that the simultaneous use of resources inside and outside the ARIN region (such as anycast, or similar geographically diverse use cases) may be included in staff’s interpretation of out-of-region use, which does not appear to be intended. This proposal is intended to address that concern.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Internet2 Technology Exchange</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/Internet2-TechEx2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/Internet2-TechEx2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The 2026 Internet2 Technology Exchange (TechEX26) is the premier annual technical event for the global research and education (R&amp;amp;E) community. This is where chief technologists, engineers, cloud architects, security analysts, IAM professionals, researchers, and more come together to solve real-world challenges.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;TechEX26 delivers interactive sessions, hands-on learning, working meetings, and unconference experiences that bridge the strategic and operational. Expect practical takeaways that you can apply immediately, plus meaningful collaboration with peers and industry experts who understand the R&amp;amp;E environment.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CITEL 49 Meeting of PCC.I</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/CITEL49/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/CITEL49/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;CITEL (Inter‑American Telecommunication Commission), as part of the Organization of American States (OAS), is one of the many RTO (regional telecommunications organizations) which provides input into the International Telecommunications Union (ITU) process (standards and resolutions).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Nate Davis, Senior Government Affairs Analyst, and Greg Staff, Government Affairs Analyst, will be attending this meeting in preparation for the ITU Plenipotentiary meeting taking place in November 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ITU Plenipotentiary Conference</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/ITUPC2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/ITUPC2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The International Telecommunication Union (ITU) is the United Nations specialized agency for information and communication technologies (ICTs). The Plenipotentiary Conference (PP), ITU’s highest policy-making body, meets once every four years to set the ITU’s general policies, adopt the four-year strategic and financial plans, and elect the senior management team of the organization, the Member States of the Council, and the members of the Radio Regulations Board. The next Plenipotentiary Conference (PP-22) will be held in Doha, Qatar, 9-27 November 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ITU World Telecommunication/Information and Communication Technology Policy Forum (WTPF)</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/ITU-WTPF2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/ITU-WTPF2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;WTPF brings together governments, industry, academia, civil society, and the technical community to exchange perspectives, explore emerging policy issues, and contribute to shaping international dialogue on the future of telecommunication and ICT policy. WTPF is designed as a forum for open dialogue, enabling stakeholders from across the global technology ecosystem to share insights and help inform international policy discussions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ITU-T Study Group 2 (SG2) Meeting</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/ITU-T-SG2-2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/ITU-T-SG2-2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;SG2 is the ITU’s authority on international numbering, naming, addressing, and identification (NNAI) and is responsible for the International Numbering Resource (INR) Database. ARIN’s Einar Bohlin, Vice President, Government Affairs, and Christine Kim, Government Affairs Analyst, will be attending in person in Geneva, Switzerland.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ASO AC Delivers Recommended Draft RIR Governance Document to NRO EC</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260728/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260728/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net/about/executive-council/&#34;&gt;Number Resource Organization Executive Council (NRO EC)&lt;/a&gt; is pleased to announce that the Address Supporting Organization Address Council (ASO AC), which fulfills the role of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net/about/address-supporting-organization/the-nro-number-council/&#34;&gt;Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC)&lt;/a&gt;, has completed its work on version 3 of the RIR Governance Document.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This work was undertaken by the ASO AC in response to the NRO EC’s request to review and update &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.icann.org/resources/pages/new-rirs-criteria-2012-02-25-en&#34;&gt;Internet Coordination Policy-2 (ICP-2): Criteria for Establishment of New Regional Internet Registries&lt;/a&gt;, and to support a strengthened governance framework for the Regional Internet Registry (RIR) system.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Features Added to ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260728-release/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260728-release/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is pleased to present the latest version of ARIN Online, including improvements, new features, and updates. Full release notes are included at the end of this message.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our work on this release has been completed, and all ARIN systems are operating normally. We thank you for your patience. If you have additional questions, comments, or issues, please submit an Ask ARIN ticket using your ARIN Online account or call the Registration Services Help Desk at +1.703.227.0660 during business hours (Monday through Friday, 7:00 AM to 7:00 PM ET).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Internet Governance Forum USA</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/IGFUSA2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/IGFUSA2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The Internet Governance Forum USA (IGF-USA) is a multistakeholder effort to illuminate issues and cultivate constructive discussions about the future of the Internet. It provides a domestic forum in the US to engage civil society, government, technologists, research scientists, industry and academia, helping to create partnerships, coalitions and dialogues that demonstrate best practices and help move policy forward.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Don’t Get Your Wires Crossed: Appropriate Use Cases for IPv6-Only vs. IPv6-Mostly</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/07/21/ipv6-mostly/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:00:35 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/07/21/ipv6-mostly/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;a-matter-of-terminology&#34;&gt;A Matter of Terminology&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IETF terminology is often not clearly and explicitly defined, leading to confusion and uses of terms not originally intended by the standards. That inappropriate use can even affect the quality of service offered to the user.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Terms like IPv6-only and IPv6-mostly are a clear example of this. Despite the complexity of reaching a consensus on definitions, v6ops is finally making progress with the &lt;a href=&#34;https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-v6ops-ipv6-only/&#34;&gt;draft-ietf-v6ops-ipv6-only Working Group document&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meeting of the ARIN Advisory Council - 16 July 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0716/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0716/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Teleconference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;col&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card panel-style panel-info&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-header&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h2 class=&#34;card-title&#34;&gt;Draft Minutes&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;These minutes are DRAFT. They have been reviewed by the ARIN Advisory Council prior to posting. These minutes will remain draft until they are reviewed and approved by the ARIN Advisory Council at their next regularly scheduled meeting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-ac-attendees&#34;&gt;ARIN AC Attendees:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kat Hunter, Chair (KH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lily Botsyoe (LB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;E. Marie Brierley (EMB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Doug Camin, Vice Chair (DC)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gerry George (GG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Elizabeth Goodson (EG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Brian Jones (BJ)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kaitlyn Pellak (KP)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gus Reese (GR)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Leif Sawyer (LS)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alicia Trotman (AT)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Matthew Wilder (MW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Woodfield (CW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alison Wood (AW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-staff&#34;&gt;ARIN Staff:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Curran, President &amp;amp; CEO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Eddie Diego, Policy Analyst&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Jennifer Lee, Deputy General Counsel&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lisa Liedel, Director, RSD&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Thérèse  Simcox, Sr. E.A./Scribe&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Sweeting, CXO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Joe Westover, Sr. Director, CXS&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;regrets&#34;&gt;Regrets:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;William Herrin (WH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;observers&#34;&gt;Observers:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Nancy Carter, ARIN Board Chair&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-welcome-and-roll-call&#34;&gt;1. Welcome and Roll Call.&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Chair called the meeting to order at 4:02 p.m. ET. The presence of a quorum was noted via roll call. The Chair acknowledged regrets from WH and welcomed ARIN Board Chair, Nancy Carter. It was noted that GG was having technical difficulties with audio but was present at the meeting.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Scheduled System Maintenance – 28 July</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260714/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260714/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN will be performing maintenance on our systems on Tuesday, 28 July, from 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM ET.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;During this window, the following services will be unavailable:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;ARIN Online&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;RESTful Provisioning service&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI) Up/Down service&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;RPKI Repository Publication service&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any RESTful calls sent during this window will be queued but may need to be resubmitted after the maintenance period.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The following services will continue to be operational during this window, but no updates will be published:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN-prop-352: Harmonize Section 1 and Section 6, Principles and Goals Statements</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_352/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_352/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-statement&#34;&gt;Problem Statement&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are two main sections of the NRPM that discuss principles and goals; one is found in Section 1, and the other in Section 6; similar language in Section 4 has been previously retired. Given the history of these two sections, there are multiple redundancies and incongruities in their language. This proposal seeks to clarify the language of both sections in order to better communicate ARIN’s principles and goals.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN’s IPv6 Fee Waiver expires 31 December 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260709/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260709/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As part of the 2022 Fee Schedule, ARIN established a five-year IPv6 Fee Waiver that allowed organizations in the 3X-Small service category to receive up to a /36 of total IPv6 space without moving up to the larger 2X-Small billing category. The waiver was intended as a time-bound incentive to support IPv6 adoption among smaller organizations and is scheduled to expire on 31 December 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Beginning 1 January 2027, organizations will be billed according to the applicable Registration Services Plan service category based on their aggregate Internet number resource holdings. For organizations currently benefiting from the IPv6 Fee Waiver, this may result in a move from the 3X-Small billing category to the 2X-Small billing category.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Apply Today for the ARIN 58 Fellowship Program</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/07/08/arin-58-fellowship-applications/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 08 Jul 2026 05:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/07/08/arin-58-fellowship-applications/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The call for applications to the ARIN 58 &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/fellowships/&#34;&gt;Fellowship Program&lt;/a&gt; is out! We are excited to once again welcome selected Fellows to our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/upcoming/&#34;&gt;Public Policy and Members Meeting&lt;/a&gt;, this time taking place in Miami, Florida, in late October.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For more than 16 years, the ARIN Fellowship Program has played a vital role in our community by broadening engagement and helping newcomers better understand the work we do at ARIN. For ARIN 58, Fellows will follow a customized learning program led by community experts and ARIN staff, designed to enhance their understanding of the complexities of ARIN and their role in Internet number resource policies.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Apply Today for the ARIN 58 Fellowship Program</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260706/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260706/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Interested in Internet governance, number resource policy, and getting involved in the ARIN community? Become an ARIN Fellow! Applications for the ARIN 58 Fellowship Program are now open, and we encourage you to apply for this specialized, interactive learning opportunity.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/beafellow&#34;&gt;Apply Today!&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Applications are now being accepted through 19 July 2026. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-to-expect&#34;&gt;What to Expect&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Selected Fellows will participate in virtual sessions before and after the ARIN 58 Public Policy and Members Meeting held 22-23 October 2026 in Miami, Florida, and online. Fellows may attend ARIN 58 either in person or virtually, as determined by the Fellowship Selection Committee.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>IPv4 Waiting List Distribution</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260702/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260702/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On Thursday, 2 July 2026, ARIN fulfilled 307 requests off the IPv4 Waiting List from the 199 IPv4 blocks listed on the IPv4 Addresses Cleared for Waiting List page:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/blocks_cleared/&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/blocks_cleared/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Prior inferences about the reputation of these address blocks, causing these blocks to be placed on a blocklist, are most likely no longer valid. For more information about ARIN’s IPv4 Waiting List Availability Process, please see our blog post from the ARIN Blog:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
