    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Nomination Period for ARIN Elections Closes Monday, 22 June</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260617-nominations/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260617-nominations/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN would like to remind the community that we are currently accepting self-nominations now through Monday, 22 June, at 7:00 PM ET to fill the following positions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three seats for the ARIN Board of Trustees:&lt;/strong&gt; Elected individuals will serve three-year terms starting 1 January 2027. Submit your self-nomination at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026Board-Nom&#34;&gt;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026Board-Nom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Five seats for the ARIN AC:&lt;/strong&gt; Elected individuals will serve three-year terms starting 1 January 2027. Submit your self-nomination at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026AC-Nom&#34;&gt;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026AC-Nom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One seat for the NRO NC:&lt;/strong&gt; Nominees will be considered for appointment by the ARIN Board for a three-year term beginning 1 January 2027. Submit your self-nomination at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026NRONC-Nom&#34;&gt;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2026NRONC-Nom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;nomination-information&#34;&gt;Nomination Information&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Self-nominations are required for all open seats. You may only stand for election for one position; please review the specific qualifications and responsibilities when considering your selection:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sponsorship Opportunities Available for ARIN 58</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260616/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260616/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Sponsorship opportunities are now available for our upcoming Public Policy and Members Meeting, ARIN 58, being held on 22-23 October in Miami, Florida.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN meetings provide an opportunity for the Internet community to engage in policy discussions, network with colleagues, and learn more about the Regional Internet Registry and issues affecting the global Internet numbers community. Sponsoring this event is a great way for your organization to:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Showcase your leadership in the Internet ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Amplify your brand to an influential and engaged audience.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Support the transparent, community-driven policy development processes that support the foundation of Internet infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If your organization is interested in sponsoring ARIN 58, please visit &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.net/sponsorship&#34;&gt;https://arin.net/sponsorship&lt;/a&gt; for details on the costs and sponsor benefits. We offer a range of sponsorship packages, each designed to provide high-value exposure, recognition, and direct engagement with the ARIN community and to meet your organization’s objectives and budget.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN-prop-351: NRPM Section 6.4.1 Retirement</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_351/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_351/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-statement&#34;&gt;Problem Statement&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Current NRPM Section 6.4.1 contains language referring to property rights of IPv6 direct allocations made by ARIN.  Past references to any rights on IP resources was defined in legacy versions of the Resource Services Agreement between an entity and ARIN.  Any mention of property or other rights do not belong in the Number Resource Policy Manual, this should be referenced in the Registration Services Agreement.  Section 6 of the Number Resource Policy Manual was modeled on a framework the other RIRs added to their policy manuals going back as far as 2004.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ready to Run? Your Guide to ARIN Elections Nominations</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/06/10/nominations-guide/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 10 Jun 2026 13:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/06/10/nominations-guide/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Are you ready to help shape the future of Internet number resource policy? Each year, ARIN community members step up to serve on our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/board&#34;&gt;Board of Trustees&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ac&#34;&gt;Advisory Council (AC)&lt;/a&gt; and on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/nronc&#34;&gt;Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC)&lt;/a&gt;. This year, the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260608-nominations/&#34;&gt;Call for Nominations&lt;/a&gt; opened 8 June and closes at 7:00 PM ET on 22 June. Here&amp;rsquo;s what you need to know.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-run&#34;&gt;Why Run?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Serving on the ARIN Board or AC isn&amp;rsquo;t just a résumé line. It&amp;rsquo;s a meaningful opportunity to protect a shared global resource. The volunteers who guide ARIN&amp;rsquo;s policy development and strategic direction help determine how the Internet&amp;rsquo;s number resources are managed across the region and support global Internet governance. If you care about a secure, stable, and accessible Internet, this is how you help build it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Nominations Now Open for the ARIN Board of Trustees, ARIN Advisory Council, and NRO Number Council</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260608-nominations/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260608-nominations/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is pleased to announce that self-nominations are now open for the 2026 ARIN Elections for the ARIN Board of Trustees, ARIN Advisory Council (AC), or the Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC). Active participation in ARIN governance and the Internet number resource Policy Development Process is essential for ARIN to maintain a robust and transparent registry.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We are accepting self-nominations beginning Monday, 8 June, through 7:00 PM ET on Monday, 22 June, for the following:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>We Want to Hear from You: Take ARIN&#39;s 2026 Customer Satisfaction Survey</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/28/customer-satisfaction-survey/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 28 May 2026 09:15:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/28/customer-satisfaction-survey/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At ARIN, we believe that a registry truly serves its community only when it listens to that community. That&amp;rsquo;s why, along with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/blog/2022/09/21/listening-to-feedback/&#34;&gt;the many other ways we collect your feedback&lt;/a&gt;, we pause every three years to ask you directly: How are we doing?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Today, we&amp;rsquo;re launching our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/customersurvey4&#34;&gt;2026 Customer Satisfaction Survey&lt;/a&gt; — and we&amp;rsquo;re inviting you to take about 15 minutes to share your honest thoughts on our services, tools, staff, and overall performance. The survey is open now through 19 June, and your input will directly shape how we prioritize improvements in the years ahead.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026 ARIN Customer Satisfaction Survey Now Open</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260528/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 28 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260528/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN has launched our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/customersurvey&#34;&gt;Customer Satisfaction Survey&lt;/a&gt; to better understand how well we are meeting the needs of our customers and the broader Internet community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The survey is open beginning today, 28 May, and will run through Friday, 19 June.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/customersurvey1&#34;&gt;Take the 2026 Customer Survey&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Working with marketing research firm Radius Insights, we developed this survey to gather feedback on ARIN’s services and operations, including Technical Services, Registration and Financial Services, Policy Development, Communications, outreach, and community engagement.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Your Vote Shapes the Internet: Why General Membership Matters in 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/27/general-membership-2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 27 May 2026 10:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/27/general-membership-2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At ARIN, the organizations we serve are more than customers — they are members of the community that manages and maintains a foundational layer of the Internet. Every IP address block and Autonomous System Number in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/region/&#34;&gt;ARIN region&lt;/a&gt; exists within a framework of policy that is shaped not by ARIN staff but by our community, through a transparent, bottom-up process. That process only works when people participate.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The 2026 &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/elections&#34;&gt;ARIN Elections&lt;/a&gt; are scheduled for 22–30 October. Three seats on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/board&#34;&gt;Board of Trustees&lt;/a&gt; and five seats on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ac&#34;&gt;Advisory Council&lt;/a&gt; will be determined by votes cast by General Member organizations. (This year, the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/nronc&#34;&gt;NRO Number Council&lt;/a&gt; seat is appointed rather than elected.) If your organization holds Internet number resources under an &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/agreements/#registration-services-agreement&#34;&gt;ARIN Agreement&lt;/a&gt;, you may already be eligible to become a General Member — and the path to participation is simpler than you might expect.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Features Added to ARIN Online</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260526/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 26 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260526/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is pleased to present the latest version of ARIN Online, including improvements, new features, and updates. Full release notes are included at the end of this message.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our work on this release has been completed, and all ARIN systems are operating normally. We thank you for your patience. If you have additional questions, comments, or issues, please submit an Ask ARIN ticket using your ARIN Online account or call the Registration Services Help Desk at +1.703.227.0660 during business hours (Monday through Friday, 7:00 AM to 7:00 PM ET).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Nine Lives of an Early Adopter: ESnet’s IPv6 Journey — and Why It Matters Now</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/22/arin-57-keynote-nine-lives-ipv6/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 22 May 2026 08:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/22/arin-57-keynote-nine-lives-ipv6/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt; Public Policy and Members Meeting, held 19-22 April 2026 in Louisville, Kentucky, and online, featured a keynote address that brought three decades of real-world &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ipv6&#34;&gt;IPv6&lt;/a&gt; experience to bear on the question the Internet community keeps asking: Are we there yet?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Inder Monga, Executive Director of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.es.net/&#34;&gt;ESnet&lt;/a&gt;, and Nick Buraglio, a member of the Planning and Architecture team at ESnet and co-chair of the IPv6 operations group within the IETF, joined the meeting virtually to deliver “The Nine Lives of an Early Adopter: Leading Cats to Water in the IPv6 Era.” Their presentation drew a compelling through line from ESnet’s earliest involvement with IPv6 in the mid-1990s to the practical realities — and opportunities — of IPv6-only deployments happening right now.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
