    <item>
      <title>Meeting of the ARIN Advisory Council - 21 May 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0521/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0521/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Teleconference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-ac-attendees&#34;&gt;ARIN AC Attendees:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kat Hunter, Chair (KH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lily Botsyoe (LB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;E. Marie Brierley (EMB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Doug Camin, Vice Chair (DC)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gerry George (GG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Elizabeth Goodson (EG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;William Herrin (WH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kaitlyn Pellak (KP)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gus Reese (GR)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Leif Sawyer (LS)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alicia Trotman (AT)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Matthew Wilder (MW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alison Wood (AW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Woodfield (CW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-staff&#34;&gt;ARIN Staff:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Eddie Diego, Policy Analyst&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Richard Jimmerson, COO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Jennifer Lee, Deputy General Counsel&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lisa Liedel, Director, RSD&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alyssa Arceneaux, Board Ops. Mgr./Scribe&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Joe Westover, Sr. Director CXS&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;regrets&#34;&gt;Regrets:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Brian Jones&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-welcome-and-roll-call&#34;&gt;1.&#x9;Welcome and Roll Call.&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Chair called the meeting to order at 4:03 p.m. ET. The presence of a quorum was noted via roll call. She welcomed everyone to the call and acknowledged regrets from Brian Jones.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Memorial Day Closing Information</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260521/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260521/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The ARIN office will close early on Friday, 22 May, and be closed on Monday, 25 May, in observance of Memorial Day. On 22 May, the main office and Financial Services Help Desk will close at 3:00 PM ET and the Registration Services Help Desk will close at 3:30 PM ET.  ARIN’s office will reopen with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/contact/#operating-hours&#34;&gt;normal operating hours&lt;/a&gt; on Tuesday, 26 May.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Has a Testing Environment — and Most People Don&#39;t Know About It</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/19/operational-testing-and-evaluation-environment/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 19 May 2026 10:20:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/19/operational-testing-and-evaluation-environment/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At last month’s &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt; Public Policy and Members Meeting, an RPKI &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/outreach/arin_by_request/#deep-dive&#34;&gt;Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt; workshop attendee asked me an important question — but it wasn&amp;rsquo;t about the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/rpki&#34;&gt;Resource Public Key Infrastructure&lt;/a&gt;. It was something simpler: He didn&amp;rsquo;t know ARIN had a testing environment. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;He&amp;rsquo;s not alone. If it’s news to you, too, read on to learn about this valuable and easy-to-access tool. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-ot-e&#34;&gt;What Is OT&amp;amp;E?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/reference/tools/testing/&#34;&gt;Operational Test and Evaluation (OT&amp;amp;E) environment&lt;/a&gt; is not a limited preview or a stripped-down demo. It offers full feature parity with production — same services, same interface, same data structure — but completely isolated from live systems. Anything you do in OT&amp;amp;E stays in OT&amp;amp;E.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
