    <item>
      <title>Midwest Peering Summit</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/MWPS2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/MWPS2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The Midwest Peering Summit (MWPS) is a regional Internet infrastructure and networking conference focused on peering, interconnection, broadband, and data center collaboration across the Midwest. The 2026 event takes place July 8 in Des Moines, Iowa, bringing together ISPs, Internet exchanges (IXPs), cloud and content providers, carriers, network engineers, and infrastructure leaders.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why IPv6, Why Now? The Operational and Business Case for Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;9:00-10:00 AM CT&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;John Sweeting, ARIN Chief Experience Officer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Rodney Payne</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/author/rodney-payne/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 14 May 2026 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/author/rodney-payne/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;An ARIN 57 Fellow pursuing active “re-tyrement,” Rodney remains deeply committed to advancing Caribbean development. He is dedicated to strengthening community participation and passionate about closing the digital divide across the region.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Community That Changed How I See the Internet</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/14/fellowship-experience-rodney-payne/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 14 May 2026 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/14/fellowship-experience-rodney-payne/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Being selected as an &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/03/10/arin-57-fellows/&#34;&gt;ARIN 57 Fellow&lt;/a&gt; was both an honor and an eye‑opening experience. Attending my first &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN meeting in Louisville, Kentucky&lt;/a&gt;, marked a turning point in how I understand the Internet — not just as technology, but as a living, collaborative ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;from-user-to-steward&#34;&gt;From User to Steward&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;With more than 30 years of experience in ICT, I believed I had a solid grasp of how the Internet works. I quickly realized how much more there was to learn. Before ARIN 57, the Internet was something I consumed through an ISP. After the meeting, I began to see it as something we can — and must — actively participate in shaping.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Fee Increase Approved for 2027</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260512/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260512/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At its meeting on 19 April, and in conformance with the Registration Services Plan (RSP) fee schedule, the Board of Trustees approved a 5 percent increase to RSP fees for 2027.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The new fee schedule is available at: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/fees/images/2027feeschedule.pdf&#34;&gt;2027 Fee Schedule&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This change was approved to support ARIN’s long-term financial strategy, which aims to align operating costs with revenues while maintaining tight cost control targets for the organization through 2030.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you have questions, please contact &lt;a href=&#34;mailto:fee-inquiries@arin.net&#34;&gt;fee-inquiries@arin.net&lt;/a&gt; or submit via Ask ARIN while logged in to your ARIN Online account.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Demystifying RPKI: New Tools to Simplify ROA Planning and Visualize Validation</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/11/arin-57-keynote-demystifying-rpki/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 11 May 2026 12:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/11/arin-57-keynote-demystifying-rpki/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt; Public Policy and Members Meeting, held 19-22 April 2026 in Louisville, Kentucky, and online, featured a keynote address that offered something extremely valuable in the routing security world: practical tools built by someone who spends his days helping real network operators improve routing integrity. &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/blog/author/steven-wallace/&#34;&gt;Steve Wallace&lt;/a&gt;, Director of Routing Integrity at &lt;a href=&#34;https://internet2.edu/&#34;&gt;Internet2&lt;/a&gt;, delivered “Demystifying RPKI: Exploring Tools to Simplify ROA Planning and Visualize Validation” shortly after the meeting opened on Monday morning. His presentation introduced a suite of openly accessible web-based tools developed through &lt;a href=&#34;https://internet2.edu/caida-and-internet2-collaborate-to-strengthen-re-routing-security/&#34;&gt;a collaboration&lt;/a&gt; between Internet2 and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.caida.org/&#34;&gt;CAIDA&lt;/a&gt;, funded in part by &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nsf.gov/funding&#34;&gt;National Science Foundation grant&lt;/a&gt; OAC-2530871 and designed to make &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/rpki&#34;&gt;Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI)&lt;/a&gt; more approachable — and safer — for network operators of all sizes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add IRR Object Action Logging Equal to the ROA Action Logging</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-09/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 11 May 2026 09:55:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-09/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;19 May 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2026.9 upon confirmed receipt, requesting that ARIN add the action logging for Internet Routing Registry (IRR) objects to match the logging functionality available for Route Origin Authorizations (ROAs).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree this feature would benefit customers that need to track IRR object actions.  We are adding this suggestion to our routing security roadmap for future development.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your suggestion has been referred to our internal process for prioritization and implementation planning and is now closed. Thank you for participating in ARIN’s Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RIR Governance Document Version 2 Status Report May 2026 Now Available</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260508/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 08 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260508/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net/about/address-supporting-organization/the-nro-number-council/&#34;&gt;Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC)&lt;/a&gt; has updated the Q1 Status Report based on discussions held during the in‑person meetings at ICANN 85.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.nro.net/wp-content/uploads/RIR-Governance-Document-Version-2-Status-Report-Q1-2026.pdf&#34;&gt;Q1 Status Report&lt;/a&gt; built on the outcomes of the NRO NC workshop held from 12 to 14 November 2025 in Montevideo. That workshop reviewed feedback received across the five RIR mailing lists, as well as input submitted through webinars and online sessions, RIR meetings, community fora, engagement with ICANN communities, and the ICANN Public Comment process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meet the 2026 Nomination Committee</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260506/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260506/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We are pleased to announce that Andrew Dul, Brian Jones, and John Stitt have been selected to join the 2026 Nomination Committee (NomCom). They are joining the appointed Board members and the community representatives serving since last year.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The 2026 NomCom is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Peter Harrison, Chair and Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Rob Seastrom, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Tacit, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Christopher Quesada, General Member representative &lt;sup&gt;(1)&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;William Sylvester, General Member representative &lt;sup&gt;(1)&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Andrew Dul, General Member representative &lt;sup&gt;(2)&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Brian Jones, General Member representative &lt;sup&gt;(2)&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Stitt, General Member representative &lt;sup&gt;(2)&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;/sup&gt; Term is for 2025–2026 Election Cycles&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; Term is for 2026–2027 Election Cycles&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CaribNOG 31: Strengthening the Caribbean’s Digital Resilience</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/05/caribnog-31/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 15:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/05/caribnog-31/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Across the Caribbean, the conversation about digital infrastructure has changed. Issues once treated primarily as technical matters now command the attention of ministers, regulators, national security advisors, and development institutions. CaribNOG 31 — the 31st regional meeting of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.caribnog.org/&#34;&gt;Caribbean Network Operators Group&lt;/a&gt;, convened in Kingston, Jamaica, on 14-16 April 2026 — expressed that shift with particular clarity.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;caribnog-group.png&#34; alt=&#34;Assembled leadership pictured at CaribNOG 31&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-resilience-requirement-hits-home&#34;&gt;The Resilience Requirement Hits Home&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hosted at the Jamaica Pegasus Hotel under the theme “The Resilient Archipelago: Strengthening the Caribbean’s Digital Core,” the meeting brought together more than 100 network operators, Internet community partners, government officials, regulators, and next-generation practitioners for three days of highly interactive discussions, training, and working sessions on digital sovereignty and critical Internet infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/ARIN58/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/ARIN58/</guid>
      <description>&lt;!-- content optional --&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Meeting Report Now Available</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260505/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260505/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting Report, including presentations, links to daily recaps on the ARIN Blog, transcripts, and webcast archives, is now available on the ARIN website at &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.net/ARIN57&#34;&gt;https://arin.net/ARIN57&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN would like to thank everyone who participated in ARIN 57, whether at home or in person in Louisville, Kentucky. Special thanks to our network sponsor, Spectrum; platinum sponsor, Amazon Web Services; silver sponsor, IPXO; and espresso bar host, Verisign, for helping make ARIN 57 possible.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Apply for a 2026 ARIN Community Grant</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/04/grant-applications-open/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 11:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/05/04/grant-applications-open/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At ARIN, we don’t take the health and growth of the Internet for granted, which is why we launched the ARIN Community Grant Program in 2019. Now entering its eighth year, the program provides financial support for operational and research projects that improve the Internet industry and user environment. To date, it has funded 26 projects, awarding a total of nearly US$350,000. And now it could be your turn to receive financial, networking, and logistical support for a project that benefits the ARIN community.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN-prop-350: NRPM Section 6.5 Revision</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_350/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/policy/proposals/2026/ARIN_prop_350/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-statement&#34;&gt;Problem Statement&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Current NRPM Section 6.5 contains allocation mechanisms that are complex and formula driven. These mechanisms include rigid sizing calculations, utilization-based thresholds, and IPv4-dependent qualification criteria.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IPv6 deployment is based on hierarchical planning, aggregation, and projected growth.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN’s IPv6 network planning guide emphasizes structured planning instead of mathematical formulas, including the use of hierarchical addressing, aggregation, and multi-year growth projections.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The current policy is complex, is difficult for applicants to interpret consistently and does not align with ARIN’s published guidance.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Lowercase IPv6 in Networks CSV per RFC 5952</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-08/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Apr 2026 09:55:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-08/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11 May 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2026.8 upon confirmed receipt, requesting that ARIN update the format of IPv6 networks in the downloadable CSV to lowercase as recommended by RFC 5952.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree that this would provide a more standardized and readable report.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your suggestion has been referred to our internal process for prioritization and implementation planning and is now closed. Thank you for participating in ARIN’s Consultation and Suggestion Process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Allow Customers with Reallocated Resources to Create ROAs</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-07/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2026 09:55:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-07/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;26 May 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2026.7 upon confirmed receipt, requesting a progress update on ARIN plans to allow customers with reallocated resources to create ROAs.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is connected to a suggestion submitted by another ARIN customer in 2023: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2023/2023-08/&#34;&gt;Suggestion 2023.8&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The prior suggestion was closed with the commitment to conduct a Community Consultation on a proposed solution after investigating the options and implications for adding this functionality.  Due to competing priorities, we are still in the process of investigating the options and will be taking your suggestion into account now.  We will be hosting that consultation in the coming months.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
