    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting, Day 1 Transcript - Monday, 20 April 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day1_transcript/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day1_transcript/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  This transcript may contain errors due to errors in transcription or in formatting it for posting. Therefore, the material is presented only to assist you, and is not an authoritative representation of discussion at the meeting. If additional clarification and details are required, videos from our original webcast are available on our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/user/teamarin&#34;&gt;YouTube channel&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;opening-and-announcements&#34;&gt;Opening and Announcements&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hollis Kara:&lt;/strong&gt; All right. All right. Okay. Kind of waiting for the line to drain on the coffee bar. I know that&amp;rsquo;s an exciting addition for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting, Day 2 Transcript - Tuesday, 21 April 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day2_transcript/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day2_transcript/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  This transcript may contain errors due to errors in transcription or in formatting it for posting. Therefore, the material is presented only to assist you, and is not an authoritative representation of discussion at the meeting. If additional clarification and details are required, videos from our original webcast are available on our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/user/teamarin&#34;&gt;YouTube channel&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;opening-and-announcements&#34;&gt;Opening and Announcements&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hollis Kara:&lt;/strong&gt; We&amp;rsquo;re going to get this party started. I hope everyone had a wonderful time at the Louisville Slugger Museum last night, and we&amp;rsquo;re glad you&amp;rsquo;re back today.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting, Day 3 Transcript - Wednesday, 22 April 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day3_transcript/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/day3_transcript/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;card well&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;card-body&#34;&gt;&#xA;  This transcript may contain errors due to errors in transcription or in formatting it for posting. Therefore, the material is presented only to assist you, and is not an authoritative representation of discussion at the meeting. If additional clarification and details are required, videos from our original webcast are available on our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/user/teamarin&#34;&gt;YouTube channel&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;opening-and-announcements&#34;&gt;Opening and Announcements&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hollis Kara:&lt;/strong&gt; It&amp;rsquo;s Wednesday.  And folks are, as I said, the elevators are slow and busy this morning, and we have folks coming down from 25. So I expect they&amp;rsquo;ll be trickling into the room. But let&amp;rsquo;s get started for the benefit of those joining us online, sticking to schedule. I&amp;rsquo;d like to welcome you to day three of ARIN 57.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Calling All General Members - Grant Selection Committee Applications Extended until 1 May</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260424-grantcom/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260424-grantcom/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN relies on General Members to support organizational governance through participation in elections and various program committees.  Your involvement in our Grant Selection Committee is needed to ensure that the ARIN Community Grant Program can evaluate and select grant applications that will provide the most benefit to the ARIN community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We are extending our call for applications through 1 May for two representatives from ARIN’s General Members to serve on the 2026 Grant Selection Committee.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Scheduled Billing System Maintenance – 1-2 May</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260424/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260424/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN will be performing maintenance on its billing systems from 8:00 PM ET on Friday, 1 May, until 4:00 PM ET, on Saturday, 2 May.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;During this time, customers may not be able to view, download, or pay invoices.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;All other ARIN services will remain available.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We appreciate your patience during this maintenance window.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Mark Kosters&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;Chief Technology Officer&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;ARIN&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Add Optional Flags for ROA Creation Notifications</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-06/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2026 09:55:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-06/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;27 April 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2026.6 upon confirmed receipt, requesting that ARIN add optional flags for ROA creation notifications.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We agree that the suggestion to allow for configuration of the notifications for ROA creations would permit a more streamlined and customizable experience for users of ARIN’s RPKI services.  As noted in your suggestion, this would be an enhancement to the feature request in suggestion 2025.6: Disable Option for Bulk ROA Removal Notifications. Your suggested enhancements have been grouped with other pending ROA notification improvements for future development.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Day 3 Recap</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/22/arin-57-day-3-recap/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2026 12:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/22/arin-57-day-3-recap/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We’ve concluded the third and final day of the ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting! A big thank you to all who participated in person and virtually and helped make this another productive and engaging event. To reference anything you’ve seen at the meeting, visit our &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57materials&#34;&gt;meeting materials page&lt;/a&gt;. Over the coming days, links to the full transcript and webcasts will be added to this page as well. In the meantime, here’s an overview of what happened on day three — a focused half-day of department reports, outreach highlights, a look at registry integrity, a legal update, and an elections preview.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meeting of the ARIN Advisory Council - 22 April 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0422/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/about/welcome/ac/meetings/2026_0422/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Face-to-Face, Louisville, KY&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-ac-attendees&#34;&gt;ARIN AC Attendees:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kat Hunter, Chair (KH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lily Botsyoe (LB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;E. Marie Brierley (EMB)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Doug Camin, Vice Chair (DC)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gerry George (GG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Elizabeth Goodson (EG)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;William Herrin (WH)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Brian Jones (BJ)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Kaitlyn Pellak (KP) (via Zoom)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gus Reese (GR)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Leif Sawyer (LS)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alicia Trotman (AT)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Matthew Wilder (MW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alison Wood (AW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Woodfield (CW)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;arin-staff&#34;&gt;ARIN Staff:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Curran, President and CEO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Eddie Diego, Policy Analyst&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Matt Kalayjian, Assoc. General Counsel&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Jennifer Lee, Deputy General Counsel&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Lisa Liedel, Director, RSD&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Alyssa Arceneaux, Board Ops. Mgr./Scribe&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;John Sweeting, CXO&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Joe Westover, Sr. Director CXS&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;observer&#34;&gt;Observer:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Nancy Carter, Board Chair&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Tina Morris, Vice Board Chair&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Tacit, Board Secretary&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Dan Alexander, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Peter Harrison, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Rob Seastrom, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-welcome-and-roll-call&#34;&gt;1.&#x9;Welcome and Roll Call.&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Chair called the meeting to order at 12:36 p.m. ET. The presence of a quorum was noted via roll call. She welcomed everyone to the call.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Day 2 Recap</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/21/arin-57-day-2-recap/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 16:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/21/arin-57-day-2-recap/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;jeffers-belle.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Belle of Louisville by David Jeffers&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Welcome back for your day two recap of the ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting in Louisville, Kentucky, and online via Zoom. Today’s highlights included discussions of six Draft Policies, reports from ARIN Community Grant recipients, and presentations by ARIN staff. Thanks to everyone who has joined us so far — we’ll see you again tomorrow at 9 AM ET for the final day of the meeting.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Day 1 Recap</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/20/arin-57-day-1-recap/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/20/arin-57-day-1-recap/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;DJ-fireworks.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Thunder Over Louisville, photo credit David Jeffers&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Greetings from Louisville, Kentucky — home of the Louisville Slugger, the Kentucky Derby, and, just this past weekend, the spectacular Thunder Over Louisville fireworks display that lit up the Ohio River skyline. We&amp;rsquo;re thrilled to welcome both new and familiar faces joining us here in the Derby City and online for &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.swoogo.com/arin57/agenda&#34;&gt;a packed lineup&lt;/a&gt; of policy discussions, organizational updates, guest speakers, and more. Read on for a summary of what has happened so far at ARIN 57.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN 57 Begins Today</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260420/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260420/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The ARIN 57 Public Policy and Members Meeting begins today at 9:00 AM ET! Join us over the next three days at the Galt House Hotel in Louisville, Kentucky, or virtually via Zoom for policy discussions, organizational updates, and more.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It’s not too late to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ARIN57&#34;&gt;register to participate&lt;/a&gt;, or you can &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/streamARIN57&#34;&gt;tune in to the live webcast&lt;/a&gt; of the meeting to simply watch the proceedings.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;how-to-attend-the-meeting&#34;&gt;How to Attend the Meeting&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each morning during the meeting, registered participants will receive a reminder email with information about that day’s session. If you’re a virtual attendee, that email will contain the link you need to access the Zoom meeting. You may also access the webinar using the Virtual Event Hub under the Virtual Participants menu option on the ARIN 57 website at &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.net/ARIN57&#34;&gt;https://arin.net/ARIN57&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Making Your Voice Heard: The Future of ARIN Policy Engagement</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/16/ac-policy-engagement-survey-followup/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 16 Apr 2026 09:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/16/ac-policy-engagement-survey-followup/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Earlier this year, the ARIN Advisory Council (AC) reached out to the community with a simple but vital question: &lt;strong&gt;How can we make it easier for you to participate in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/pdp&#34;&gt;Policy Development Process (PDP)&lt;/a&gt;?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The truth is, the PDP only works when the community feels empowered to share their opinions. Policy shouldn’t feel like a closed-door meeting; it should feel like a conversation. We are excited to share the results of our recent survey and, more importantly, how the AC hopes to turn your feedback into action.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Apply Now for an ARIN Community Grant</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260416/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 16 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260416/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Do you have a project that needs funding, is noncommercial in nature, and benefits the Internet community within the ARIN service region? Apply now for a &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/community_grants/program/&#34;&gt;2026 ARIN Community Grant&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a role=&#34;button&#34; class=&#34;btn btn-primary btn-lg&#34; href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/applyforgrants&#34;&gt;2026 Grant Application&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The ARIN Community Grant Program provides financial grants in support of operational and research projects that improve the overall Internet industry and user environment, advancing ARIN’s mission and broadly benefiting the ARIN community within our region. Projects must fit into one or more of these four broad categories:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Tips and Tricks for Making the Most of ARIN 57</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/15/arin-57-tips-and-tricks/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Apr 2026 10:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/15/arin-57-tips-and-tricks/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt; is almost here — and whether you&amp;rsquo;re joining us in Louisville or logging in from your living room, a little preparation goes a long way. On Tuesday, 14 April, we held our virtual Meeting Orientation to help attendees hit the ground running. If you missed it, don&amp;rsquo;t worry. You can &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.zoom.us/rec/share/XWijwHDqJI4SBasrVPY8cKn5978HkntXaid1M2E05kyhcxhZ7223gqZ9HfhffI3n.zQojrK7wNeaQfsKI?startTime=1776189105000&#34;&gt;watch the full Zoom recording&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/materials/ARIN57_orientationpresentation.pdf&#34;&gt;view the presentation slides&lt;/a&gt;, or &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/meetings/ARIN57/materials/ARIN57_orientationguide.pdf&#34;&gt;download the Orientation Guide&lt;/a&gt; at your convenience.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Not ready to commit to the full recording? We&amp;rsquo;ve got you covered. Here&amp;rsquo;s your TL;DR guide to everything you need to know before ARIN 57 kicks off on Sunday, 19 April.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Nomination Committee Volunteers Needed</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260414/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 14 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260414/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is seeking three volunteers to serve on the Nomination Committee (NomCom) to help recruit candidates for the Board of Trustees, Advisory Council, and Number Resource Organization Number Council (NRO NC). Terms for the committee are two years.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The current members of the Nomination Committee are:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Peter Harrison, Chair&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Rob Seastrom Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chris Tacit, Trustee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Christopher Quesada, General Member representative&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;William Sylvester, General Member representative&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;General Member representative (TBD)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;General Member representative (TBD)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;General Member representative (TBD)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Volunteers must be from an ARIN General Member organization in Good Standing and may not be a candidate in an ARIN Election while serving on the committee. Chosen representatives may include at least one and up to two actively serving Advisory Council members.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Get Ready for ARIN 57</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260409/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260409/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;iframe src=&#34;//www.youtube.com/embed/mLwO9Djq_7o&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#34; allowfullscreen title=&#34;Watch at youtu.be/mLwO9Djq_7o&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ARIN is heading to Louisville, Kentucky, for ARIN 57. Our spring Public Policy and Members Meeting takes place 19-22 April 2026 at The Galt House Hotel and virtually via the Zoom webinar platform. If you haven’t registered to participate yet, it’s not too late! Visit &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/ARIN57&#34;&gt;https://arin.net/ARIN57&lt;/a&gt; to get started.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Get to Know the Draft Policies Up for Discussion at ARIN 57</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/07/arin-57-policies/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 09:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/04/07/arin-57-policies/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/arin57&#34;&gt;ARIN 57&lt;/a&gt; is almost here, and we can’t wait to gather both in person and virtually! Since ARIN 56 took place last fall, one new Draft Policy has been added to the docket, bringing us to a total of six Draft Policies to be presented at ARIN 57.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To help you prepare to engage in these important conversations, here’s a look at what&amp;rsquo;s up for discussion during the ARIN 57 &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/meetings&#34;&gt;Public Policy and Members Meeting&lt;/a&gt;, taking place 19-22 April in Louisville, Kentucky, and online. Policies will be discussed on &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.swoogo.com/arin57/agenda#:~:text=2%3A45%20PM-,Policy%20Block%20(1%2D6),-Leif%20Sawyer%20%2D%20GCI&#34;&gt;Tuesday, 21 April,&lt;/a&gt; so be sure to mark your calendar and &lt;a href=&#34;https://arin.swoogo.com/arin57/begin&#34;&gt;register today&lt;/a&gt; if you’d like to participate on site in Arlington or online via Zoom.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2025 Annual Report Now Available</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260407/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260407/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;After the close of each fiscal year, ARIN staff compiles and publishes an annual report. These reports contain information about the activities of ARIN’s staff, Board of Trustees, and Advisory Council, as well as ARIN’s activities within the global Internet community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The 2025 ARIN Annual Report is now available for download at:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/annual/reports/2025_annualreport.pdf&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/about/corporate/annual/reports/2025_annualreport.pdf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The report includes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;An overview of ARIN’s mission, services, and structure;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Updates from the President and CEO and the ARIN Board of Trustees Chair;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A summary of 2025 accomplishments from ARIN;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Departmental highlights;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;An overview of ARIN’s Policy Development Process and policy actions taken in 2025;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Activity reports from the Board of Trustees, Advisory Council, and Number Resource Organization Number Council;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A recap of the outreach and training events conducted in 2025; and&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Internet number resource statistics for 2025.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The 2025 Auditor’s Report will be posted once it becomes available.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>IPv4 Waiting List Distribution</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260403/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 03 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260403/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On Thursday, 2 April 2026, ARIN fulfilled 67 requests off the IPv4 Waiting List from the 40 IPv4 blocks listed on the IPv4 Addresses Cleared for Waiting List page:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/blocks_cleared/&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/resources/guide/ipv4/blocks_cleared/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Prior inferences about the reputation of these address blocks, causing these blocks to be placed on a blocklist, are most likely no longer valid. For more information about ARIN’s IPv4 Waiting List Availability Process, please see our blog post from the ARIN Blog:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Enable V6 for WHOWAS</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-05/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 09:55:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2026/2026-05/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;arin-comment&#34;&gt;ARIN Comment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;02 April 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your suggestion, numbered 2026.5, upon confirmed receipt, asking that ARIN add IPv6 information to the Whowas report. We agree that this would be a useful addition to Whowas, and note that it was previously suggested by another community member in 2025.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2025/2025-04/&#34;&gt;https://www.arin.net/participate/community/acsp/suggestions/2025/2025-04/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fact that this is a repeated request will be considered when evaluating prioritization of the effort to develop this improvement.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Bits: March 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/03/31/arin-bits-march-2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 09:45:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/blog/2026/03/31/arin-bits-march-2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;While spring brings fresh starts and new growth, ARIN has been cultivating both since the very beginning of 2026. Now that the season has officially sprouted, let&amp;rsquo;s dig into what&amp;rsquo;s been taking root in our community! The first three months of the year have sprouted exciting changes, updates, deployments, and more. In this edition of Bits, we share news from this past quarter and details about upcoming events, including: ARIN’s new logo; ARIN 57 and this spring’s Fellowship Program; enhanced routing security services and Point of Contact linking procedures; upcoming RPKI workshops and other industry events; and much more. Read on to learn about what’s blooming at ARIN and in our community.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>“ARIN Deep Dive — Technical Services and RPKI” is heading to Albuquerque, New Mexico!</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260331/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260331/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Join ARIN in Albuquerque, New Mexico, for our free, in-person training event — Deep Dive: Technical Services and Resource Public Key Infrastructure (RPKI). Deep Dive is designed to help you navigate our routing security tools and plunge into the practical applications of ARIN’s technical services.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Don’t miss the opportunity to immerse yourself in this expert-led session full of valuable insights and hands-on learning. We hope you’ll dive in with us and strengthen your understanding of the valuable ARIN services available to your organization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ARIN Deep Dive: Albuquerque</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/events/deepdive-abq/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/events/deepdive-abq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore the Depths of ARIN Technical Services and RPKI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Join us for our new program, ARIN Deep Dive: an educational, in-person training experience where you&amp;rsquo;ll learn how your organization can implement ARIN services such as RPKI (Resource Public Key Infrastructure) and more.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Whether you&amp;rsquo;re looking to shore up your foundational knowledge or navigate the currents of routing security, our expert-led sessions will provide you with the insights and skills you need.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Volunteer to Serve on the 2026 ARIN Grant Selection Committee</title>
      <link>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260330/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.arin.net/announcements/20260330/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;ARIN is seeking volunteers to serve on th